ags so all `#ifdef`s are already resolved. The ACTIVE body of `dtoa_r` — the real 673 lines that compile — is saved at:\n\n    /tmp/dtoa_r_active.c\n\nREAD THAT FILE FIRST. It is the definitive specification. It was produced with:\n    gcc -E -P -DHAVE_CONFIG_H -Ic_src/include -Ic_src/src c_src/src/dtoa.c\nthen extracting the `dtoa_r` function. Macro names are expanded (e.g. `word0(&u)` appears as `(&u)->L[1]`, `Exp_mask` as `0x7ff00000`, `Bias` as `0x3ff`). For readable macro names cross-reference the original `c_src/src/dtoa.c` (function starts line 5012; USE_BF96 blocks at 5072-5139, 5154-5294, 5367+, 5779+ are ACTIVE; blocks guarded `#ifndef USE_BF96` at 5139, 5294, 5306, 5813 are DEAD).\n\nNote these are NOT defined in the real build, so their branches are dead: `Sudden_Underflow`, `SET_INEXACT`, `Honor_FLT_ROUNDS`, `ROUND_BIASED`, `Check_FLT_ROUNDS`, `No_leftright`, `NO_BF96`, `NO_LONG_LONG`, `Just_16`, `VAX`, `IBM`, `IEEE_MC68k`. `IEEE_8087` (little-endian) IS defined. Also note `try_quick` does NOT exist in the active path at all.\n\n## Your task\nRewrite the body of `dtoa_r` in `src/dtoa.rs` (currently at line ~933, `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn dtoa_r`) to be a FAITHFUL, line-by-line translation of the active BF96 code in `/tmp/dtoa_r_active.c`.\n\nKeep the existing exported signature EXACTLY as-is:\n```rust\n#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\npub unsafe extern \"C\" fn dtoa_r(\n    dd: f64, mut mode: c_int, mut ndigits: c_int,\n    decpt: *mut c_int, sign: *mut c_int, rve: *mut *mut c_char,\n    buf_in: *mut c_char, blen_in: usize,\n) -> *mut c_char\n```\n\n### Helpers that ALREADY EXIST in src/dtoa.rs — reuse them, do not rewrite:\n```rust\nunsafe fn multadd(b: *mut Bigint, m: c_int, a: c_int) -> *mut Bigint   // line 204\nunsafe fn i2b(i: c_int) -> *mut Bigint                                  // line 348\nunsafe fn mult(a: *mut Bigint, b: *mut Bigint) -> *mut Bigint           // line 355\nunsafe fn pow5mult(b: *mut Bigint, k: c_int) -> *mut Bigint