d wrap. Shifts must match C exactly (watch `1ull << n`).\n- Signed `int` arithmetic stays `c_int` (i32).\n- Preserve the exact `*decpt` and `*sign` writes, the `*rve` write, the trailing-zero stripping, and the `buf`/`blen` handling (including the `blen <= (size_t)i` early-return that returns NULL and sets `*rve = buf + i` where `buf` was just set to 0 — replicate this quirk literally, including the resulting `*rve` value).\n- Keep the `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]` attribute style already used in the file (this crate is on nightly and uses `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]`).\n- Preserve the existing `dtoa` wrapper (line ~1656) which forwards to `dtoa_r`, and `freedtoa`, `gethex`, `strtod__unused` exports.\n- If parts of the old classic-path code become dead, you may delete them, BUT keep any function still referenced by other modules or by the remaining exports (`gethex`, `strtod__unused`, `jsonp_strtod` in `src/dtoa_strtod.rs`/`src/strconv.rs`). Check with grep before deleting anything.\n\n### Verify your work\n```\ncd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-QfYM1w/translated_rust\ncargo build --release 2>&1 | tail -20\ngcc -O1 -o /tmp/dd tests_c/diff_driver.c -ldl\n/tmp/dd $PWD/cbuild/libjansson.so > /tmp/c.txt\n/tmp/dd $PWD/target/release/libjansson.so > /tmp/r.txt\ndiff /tmp/c.txt /tmp/r.txt | head -40\ndiff /tmp/c.txt /tmp/r.txt | grep -c '^[<>]'\n```\nBoth files are 75420 lines. The baseline BEFORE your fix has 232 differing lines. Your goal is **0 differing lines**. Iterate until the diff is empty. Report the final differing-line count honestly — do not claim success without running this comparison.","outputFile":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-QfYM1w/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-QfYM1w-translated-rust/c1ef89ae-e696-4035-a7a9-923ffb551939/tasks/a498321f4dd04ac2c.output","canReadOutputFile":true}}
