{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_tsojynest3kal6omy3ivb5q3va4vvqhnbw3eg6g2eyydspmklu4q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have read all the files. Now producing the exhaustive inventory.\n\nKey constants confirmed: `JSON_PARSER_MAX_DEPTH 2048` (`include/jansson_config.h:10`), `JSON_ERROR_TEXT_LENGTH 160`, `JSON_ERROR_SOURCE_LENGTH 80`, `JSON_MAX_INDENT 0x1F`, `DTOA_ENABLED 1` (so the dtoa branch of `jsonp_dtostr` is live).\n\n---\n\n# Cross-cutting mechanics you must model first\n\n- `jsonp_error_vset` (`src/error.c:47`): **if `error->text[0] != '\\0'` it returns without overwriting** → the *first* error wins for the whole call. Message is `vsnprintf(text, 159, ...)`, then `text[158]='\\0'`, `text[159] = code`. So max message = 158 chars, and `json_error_code()` reads `text[159]`.\n- `error_set` (`src/load.c:85`): appends `\" near '<saved_text>'\"` **only if `saved_text[0]` non-empty AND `lex->saved_text.length <= 20`** (longer tokens get the bare message, no context). If `saved_text` is empty: code `json_error_invalid_syntax` is **silently promoted to `json_error_premature_end_of_input`**, and `\" near end of file\"` is appended unless `stream.state == STREAM_STATE_ERROR` (UTF-8 errors get no suffix).\n- `jsonp_error_set_source` truncates sources ≥80 chars to `\"...\" + tail`.\n- `jsonp_malloc(0)` returns NULL (`src/memory.c:26`) — a real error path for zero-size requests.\n\n---\n\n## src/value.c\n\n```\njsonp_loop_check | json pointer already present in `parents` hashtable (circular ref reached again) | -1 | n/a\njsonp_loop_check | hashtable_set fails (OOM) while recording pointer key | -1 (propagates hashtable_set) | n/a\njson_object | jsonp_malloc(sizeof(json_object_t)) fails | NULL | n/a\njson_object | hashtable_init fails (bucket malloc OOM); object is freed | NULL | n/a\njson_object_size | json == NULL | 0 | n/a\njson_object_size | json is any non-JSON_OBJECT type | 0 | n/a\njson_object_get | key == NULL | NULL | n/a\njson_object_get | json == NULL or not JSON_OBJECT (via getn) | NULL | n/a\njson_object_get | key absent from object | NULL | n/a\njson_object_getn | key == NULL | NULL | n/a\njson_object_getn | json == NULL or not JSON_OBJECT | NULL | n/a\njson_object_getn | key/key_len pair not present | NULL | n/a\njson_object_set_new_nocheck | key == NULL (value is decref'd) | -1 | n/a\njson_object_setn_new_nocheck | value == NULL (checked before key/type) | -1 | n/a\njson_object_setn_new_nocheck | key == NULL (value decref'd) | -1 | n/a\njson_object_setn_new_nocheck | json == NULL or not JSON_OBJECT (value decref'd) | -1 | n/a\njson_object_setn_new_nocheck | json == value (direct self-insertion, e.g. json_object_set(o,\"k\",o)) | -1 | n/a\njson_object_setn_new_nocheck | hashtable_set fails (rehash OOM, init_pair OOM, or key_len overflow) | -1 | n/a\njson_object_set_new | key == NULL | -1 | n/a\njson_object_setn_new | key == NULL | -1 | n/a\njson_object_setn_new | key is not valid UTF-8 (utf8_check_string(key,key_len)==0), e.g. \"\\xff\" | -1 | n/a\njson_object_del | key == NULL | -1 | n/a\njson_object_deln | key == NULL | -1 | n/a\njson_object_deln | json == NULL or not JSON_OBJECT | -1 | n/a\njson_object_deln | key not found in hashtable (hashtable_do_del) | -1 | n/a\njson_object_clear | json == NULL or not JSON_OBJECT | -1 | n/a\njson_object_update | `object` arg is NULL or not JSON_OBJECT | -1 | n/a\njson_object_update | `other` arg is NULL or not JSON_OBJECT | -1 | n/a\njson_object_update | inner json_object_setn_nocheck fails (e.g. other contains `object` itself, or OOM) | -1 | n/a\njson_object_update_existing | `object` NULL or not JSON_OBJECT | -1 | n/a\njson_object_update_existing | `other` NULL or not JSON_OBJECT | -1 | n/a\njson_object_update_missing | `object` NULL or not JSON_OBJECT | -1 | n/a\njson_object_update_missing | `other` NULL or not JSON_OBJECT | -1 | n/a\ndo_object_update_recursive | `object` NULL or not JSON_OBJECT | -1 |