yntax \"invalid token\" (set by parse_value)\nlex_scan_number | leading zero followed by a digit, e.g. \"[01]\", \"[-012]\" | returns -1, TOKEN_INVALID, no error set | json_error_invalid_syntax  \"invalid token near '01'\" (from parse_value)\nlex_scan_number | '-' not followed by a digit, e.g. \"[-]\", \"[-x]\", \"[-.5]\" | -1, TOKEN_INVALID | json_error_invalid_syntax  \"invalid token\"\nlex_scan_number | integer literal below json_int_t min (strtoll sets ERANGE, intval<0), e.g. \"[-9223372036854775809]\" | -1 | json_error_numeric_overflow  \"too big negative integer\"\nlex_scan_number | integer literal above json_int_t max (ERANGE, intval>=0), e.g. \"[9223372036854775808]\" | -1 | json_error_numeric_overflow  \"too big integer\"\nlex_scan_number | '.' not followed by a digit, e.g. \"[1.]\", \"[1.e5]\" | -1, TOKEN_INVALID | json_error_invalid_syntax  \"invalid token\"\nlex_scan_number | 'e'/'E' (optionally with +/-) not followed by a digit, e.g. \"[1e]\", \"[1e+]\", \"[1E-x]\" | -1, TOKEN_INVALID | json_error_invalid_syntax  \"invalid token\"\nlex_scan_number | real literal overflows double (jsonp_strtod returns -1), e.g. \"[1e999]\", \"[-1e309]\" | -1 | json_error_numeric_overflow  \"real number overflow\"\nlex_scan | alphabetic identifier that is not exactly \"true\"/\"false\"/\"null\", e.g. \"[nul]\", \"[tru]\", \"[TRUE]\", \"[foo]\" | TOKEN_INVALID | json_error_invalid_syntax  \"invalid token near 'nul'\"\nlex_scan | any other leading char (not ws, {}[]:,, \", digit, '-', alpha), e.g. \"[']\", \"[#]\", \"[@]\", \"['a']\" | TOKEN_INVALID (rest of UTF-8 seq saved) | json_error_invalid_syntax  \"invalid token near '''\"\nparse_object | json_object() fails (OOM) | NULL, no error set | n/a\nparse_object | token at key position is not TOKEN_STRING, e.g. \"{1:2}\", \"{,}\", \"{\\\"a\\\":1,}\", \"{:}\" | NULL | json_error_invalid_syntax  \"string or '}' expected\"\nparse_object | lex_steal_string returns NULL though token==TOKEN_STRING (defensive; also leaks `object`) 