40` `#define type_name(x) type_names[json_typeof(x)]` — `type_names[]` has exactly 8 entries, so an out-of-range `json_type` is an OOB read fed straight into the error message.\n\n**Duplicate keys:** only rejected in `parse_object` under `JSON_REJECT_DUPLICATES` (`json_error_duplicate_key`, \"duplicate object key\"). `json_object_set*` and default parsing silently overwrite.\n\n**Embedded NUL:** `utf8_check_first(0) == 1`, so NUL is *valid* for `json_stringn`/`json_object_setn_new`. NUL is rejected in exactly two parser places: `parse_value` (`json_error_null_character`, needs `JSON_ALLOW_NUL`) and `parse_object` (`json_error_null_byte_in_key`, **unconditional** — `JSON_ALLOW_NUL` does not help keys). Separately, `json_loads` (string_get) treats a literal NUL in the C string as EOF.\n\n**Flag validation:** none. Unknown flag bits are silently ignored; `JSON_INDENT(n)` and `JSON_REAL_PRECISION(n)` mask with `0x1F` so out-of-range values wrap instead of erroring."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1024,"cache_read_input_tokens":92505,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1024,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_0178FDBAsWWBU35GDNqZTq79","session_id":"c1ef89ae-e696-4035-a7a9-923ffb551939","uuid":"33d955ef-a4b2-4c16-a937-aa275a04fb84","timestamp":"2026-08-14T14:56:47.822Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Extract C error surface"}
