_null_character`. Independent of this flag, **object keys** containing NUL are always rejected at `load.c:684-689` (`json_error_null_byte_in_key`). |\n| depth cap | 2048 | `include/jansson_config.h:10`, checked `load.c:779-783` | `lex->depth` incremented per *value* (incl. scalars); `> 2048` ⇒ `json_error_stack_overflow`. Verified: 2047 `[` + scalar = OK; 2048 `[` + scalar = fail. `lex->depth` is *not* decremented on that error path. |\n\nUnknown/high bits are never validated anywhere — silently ignored.\n\n## 1b. Encoder flags — `src/dump.c` (all `flags &` sites)\n\n| flag | value | site | branch behavior |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `JSON_INDENT(n)` | `flags & 0x1F`, n=0..31 | `FLAGS_TO_INDENT` `dump.c:29`; used `dump.c:73-87` | n>0 ⇒ `dump(\"\\n\",1)` then `depth*n` spaces taken from `whitespace[]` (`dump.c:69`, 32 spaces) in chunks of `sizeof whitespace - 1` = **32** (`dump.c:80-86`) ⇒ `depth*n > 32` iterates the chunk loop. n==0 ⇒ falls to the `else if` at `dump.c:88`. |\n| `JSON_COMPACT` | 0x20 | `dump.c:88` and `dump.c:311-317` | `:88` — only reached when indent==0: suppresses the single space after `,`. `:311` — object separator `\":\"` vs `\": \"`, applied **regardless of indent** (verified `INDENT(4)|COMPACT` → `\"arr\":[`). |\n| `JSON_ENSURE_ASCII` | 0x40 | `dump.c:123-124` (in `dump_string`) | breaks the raw-copy loop for `codepoint > 0x7F` ⇒ escape path: BMP → `\\uXXXX` (`dump.c:166-169`), non-BMP → UTF-16 surrogate pair `\\uXXXX\\uXXXX` (`dump.c:172-182`). Without this flag the surrogate-pair branch is **unreachable**. 0x7F (DEL) is never escaped (strict `>`). |\n| `JSON_SORT_KEYS` | 0x80 | `dump.c:335-387` | malloc `struct key_len[size]`, fill from iterator, `qsort` with `compare_keys` (`dump.c:203-213`: `memcmp` over min len, tie ⇒ `len` difference ⇒ shorter-prefix-first), re-fetch each value via `json_object_getn`. Clear ⇒ `dump.c:388-413` insertion order via `ordered_list`. |\n| `JSON_PRESERVE_ORDER` | 0x100 | **declared `jansson.h:386`, referenced in ZERO `.c` files** | Complete no-op in 2.15; insertion order is always preserved. |\n| `JSON_ENCODE_ANY` | 0x200 | `dump.c:485-488` (`json_dump_callback`) | clear ⇒ root must be array or object, else return -1 before any output. |\n| `JSON_ESCAPE_SLASH` | 0x400 | `dump.c:119-120`, emit at `dump.c:161-163` | `'/'` → `\"\\/\"`. |\n| `JSON_REAL_PRECISION(n)` | `(n&0x1F)<<11` | `FLAGS_TO_PRECISION` `dump.c:30`; used `dump.c:251-252` | passed as `precision` to `jsonp_dtostr`. `strconv.c:75` `mode = precision==0 ? 0 : 2` (0 = shortest round-trip, 2 = n significant digits); `strconv.c:86` `decpt <= -4 \\|\\| decpt > 16` ⇒ exponent form; `strconv.c:101-112` returns -1 if the result would not fit ⇒ `do_dump` returns -1 ⇒ `json_dumps` returns NULL. Buffer is `MAX_REAL_STR_LENGTH`=25 (`dump.c:27`) and `digits[25]` (`strconv.c:73`). **Measured**: precision 0..17 works; 18..31 returns NULL for anything needing many digits (e.g. `0.1` fails at p25/p31; `1e-4` fails at p20). |\n| `JSON_EMBED` | 0x10000 | captured `dump.c:217`, **cleared `dump.c:219`** (so root-only, not inherited), consumed at `277, 281, 301, 324, 330, 416` | suppresses the outermost `[`/`]` or `{`/`}`. Empty array/object + EMBED ⇒ **zero bytes** output. With indent ⇒ leading and trailing `\\n` remain. |\n\nUnconditional escapes (`dump.c:115`, no flag): `\\` `\"` and every codepoint `< 0x20`; `\\b \\f \\n \\r \\t` get short forms (`dump.c:146-160`), all other control chars get `\\u00XX`. `dump_string` return value is **ignored for object keys** at `dump.c:366` and `dump.c:396` (latent upstream bug).\n\n## 1c. Pack/unpack — `src/pack_unpack.c`\n\n- `JSON_VALIDATE_ONLY` 0x1: `686, 723, 738, 753, 768, 783, 792, 797` — **unpack only**; suppresses `va_arg` consumption of value targets. Object **keys** are still consumed (`:520`). Consequence: `{s:s%}` + VALIDATE_ONLY **fails** (\"Expected format 's', got '%'\") because the `%` at `:698` is never consumed (verified).\n- `JSON_STRICT` 0x2: `:553` (object), `:658` (array) — if the container had no explicit `!`/`*`, promote to `!`.\n- `pack` never reads `s->flags` at all ⇒ both flags are inert for `json_pack_ex`/`json_vpack_ex`.\n- pack switch `:424-460` supports exactly: `{` `[` `s` `n` `b` `i` `I` `f` `O` `o`.\n- unpack switch `:672-818` supports exactly: `{` `[` `s` `i` `I` `b` `f` `F` `O` `o` `n`.\n- `unpack_value_starters = \"{[siIbfFOon\"` (`:42`), gate for array elements only (`:633`).\n- **`'r'` does not exist in this version** — neither switch nor the starters string (verified: `Unexpected format character 'r'` in both directions).\n- `'F'` is unpack-only; `'#'` is pack-only (unpack `s#` ⇒ `Expected format 's', got '#'`).\n- ignored format chars ` ` `\\t` `\\n` `,` `:` — `next_token` `:76`.\n- `#` (int len) / `%` (size_t len) / `+` (concat) — `read_string` `:131, 175, 177, 190`; `:153-159` rejects them on optional strings.\n- `?`/`*` — `pack_string :337-346`, `pack_object_inter :363-385`, `pack_object :240-256`, `pack_array :296-307`.\n- `!`/`*` — `unpack_object :508-512`, `unpack_array :627-631`; must be the last thing in the container (`:495-500`, `:614-619`).\n- `?` optional key — `unpack_object :529-532`; sets `gotopt` (`:566`) forcing the full key scan; missing optional ⇒ recursion with `root=NULL` (format-only \"skipping\" mode, `:534-537`).\n- unpack object keys use `strlen(key)` (`:525`) ⇒ keys with embedded NUL are unreachable via unpack.\n\n## 1d. Sizes / growth thresholds\n\n- `INITIAL_HASHTABLE_ORDER 3` (`hashtable.c:23-25`, `jansson_private_config.h:36`), `hashsize(n)=1<<n` (`lookup3.h:76`) ⇒ 8 buckets; rehash at `hashtable.c:234` `size >= hashsize(order)` ⇒ **the 9th distinct key rehashes to order 4**, 17th to order 5. Confirmed.\n- `hashlittle` has three code paths by key alignment (4-byte / 2-byte / unaligned, `lookup3.h:206, 290, ~335`) plus a `length>12` loop and a `switch(length)` tail for 0..12 ⇒ key lengths 0, 1-3, 4, 11, 12, 13, >24 hit distinct code.\n- Array: initial `size=8` (`value.c:438-439`); `json_array_grow` `new_size = max(size+amount, size*2)` (`value.c:519`) ⇒ 9th append → 16; a large `json_array_extend` takes the `size+amount` side.\n- `strbuffer`: `STRBUFFER_MIN_SIZE 16`, factor 2, `new_size = max(size*2, length+size+1)` (`strbuffer.c:17-19, 61-79`); measured 16→32→64.\n- `load_callback` reads in `MAX_BUF_LEN 1024` chunks (`load.c:1055`); callback returning 0 or `(size_t)-1` ⇒ EOF (`load.c:1072`). `stream_t.buffer[5]` (`load.c:57`) holds one UTF-8 sequence, refilled byte-by-byte, so chunk boundaries may split a multi-byte sequence (verified OK at chunk=1,2,3).\n- `MAX_INTEGER_STR_LENGTH 25` (`dump.c:26`) — `LLONG_MIN` is 20 chars, fits.\n- `LOOP_KEY_LEN` = `2 + sizeof(json_t*)*2 + 1` (`jansson_private.h:93`); `jsonp_loop_check` (`value.c:47-58`) keys the parents set on `\"%p\"`.\n- `utf8_encode` **accepts surrogate codepoints D800-DFFF** (`utf.c:21-25`, no range check) while `utf8_check_full` rejects them (`utf.c:99-102`) — asymmetric.\n- `json_array_append/insert/set_new` and `json_object_set*` reject `json == value` (`value.c:131, 484, 537, 560`) ⇒ direct self-cycles are impossible; only indirect cycles reach the loop checker (verified: indirect cycle ⇒ `json_dumps` NULL, `json_deep_copy` NULL; same object twice as siblings ⇒ fine).\n- `json_load_file` on success ends with `error->source == \"<stream>\"` (overwritten by `json_loadf`'s `jsonp_error_init`, `load.c:978`); only the fopen-failure path keeps the path (verified).\n\n---\n\n# Part 2 — Configuration-surface rows\n\nFormat: `entry point(s) | configuration`. Rows marked **(rejected)** are nominally-valid-looking configurations that the C actually refuses — included because a port must match the refusal.\n\n## Encoder — flag axes\n```\njson_dumps / json_dumpb / json_dumpf / json_dumpfd / json_dump_file / json_dump_callback | flags=0; root={\"arr\":[1,2],\"o\":{\"k\":null}}  (baseline: \", \" between items, \": \" after key, insertion order)\njson_dumps | flags=JSON_COMPACT (0x20); same root  (\":\" separator, no space after \",\")\njson_dumps | flags=JSON_INDENT(1); nested object+array  (newline + 1 space per level)\njson_dumps | flags=JSON_INDENT(2); nested object+array\njson_dumps | flags=JSON_INDENT(4); nested object+array\njson_dumps | flags=JSON_INDENT(31) (=JSON_MAX_INDENT); depth 1 only (31 spaces, single whitespace[] chunk)\njson_dumps | flags=JSON_INDENT(31); depth >= 2 so depth*31 > 32  (exercises the multi-chunk loop dump.c:79-87)\njson_dumps | flags=JSON_INDENT(0) explicitly  (identical to flags=0; else-branch dump.c:88)\njson_dumps | flags=JSON_INDENT(4)|JSON_COMPACT  (indent wins for newlines, COMPACT still forces \":\" not \": \")\njson_dumps | flags=JSON_ENSURE_ASCII (0x40); string with 2-byte (U+00E9), 3-byte (U+20AC) and 4-byte (U+1D11E) UTF-8  (-> \\u00E9, \\u20AC, \\uD834\\uDD1E)\njson_dumps | flags=0; same non-ASCII string  (raw UTF-8 passthrough; surrogate branch unreachable)\njson_dumps | flags=JSON_ENSURE_ASCII; string containing U+007F DEL  (NOT escaped: test is codepoint > 0x7F)\njson_dumps | flags=JSON_ESCAPE_SLASH (0x400); string \"a/b\"  (-> \"a\\/b\")\njson_dumps | flags=0; string \"a/b\"  (-> \"a/b\")\njson_dumps | flags=JSON_SORT_KEYS (0x80); object with keys inserted in non-sorted order\njson_dumps | flags=JSON_SORT_KEYS; keys where one is a prefix of another (\"a\",\"ab\")  (compare_keys tie-break on length)\njson_dumps | flags=JSON_SORT_KEYS; single-key object  (qsort with size 1)\njson_dumps | flags=JSON_SORT_KEYS; >8 keys (post-rehash iteration order vs sorted output)\njson_dumps | flags=JSON_SORT_KEYS|JSON_INDENT(2)  (sorted branch's own dump_indent calls, dump.c:373-384)\njson_dumps | flags=JSON_PRESERVE_ORDER (0x100) alone  (documented NO-OP: zero references in any .c)\njson_dumps | flags=JSON_ENCODE_ANY (0x200); root = each of string / integer / real / true / false / null\njson_dumps | flags=0; root = a scalar  (rejected: returns NULL before any output, dump.c:485-488)\njson_dumps | flags=JSON_EMBED (0x10000); root = 2-key object  ('\"x\": 1, \"y\": 2', no braces)\njson_dumps | flags=JSON_EMBED; root = 2-element array  (no brackets)\njson_dumps | flags=JSON_EMBED; root = EMPTY object or EMPTY array  (zero bytes of output)\njson_dumps | flags=JSON_EMBED|JSON_INDENT(2)  (leading and trailing newline retained)\njson_dumps | flags=JSON_EMBED; nested containers  (EMBED cleared at dump.c:219, children keep their brackets)\njson_dumps | flags=JSON_ENSURE_ASCII|JSON_ESCAPE_SLASH|JSON_SORT_KEYS|JSON_COMPACT  (all escape/order branches at once)\njson_dumps | flags = every unknown bit set (e.g. 0xFFFF0000 & ~JSON_EMBED)  (flags are never validated; ignored)\n```\n\n## Encoder — real-number / precision axes\n```\njson_dumps | JSON_REAL_PRECISION(0) (i.e. absent); 0.0, -0.0  (\"0.0\", \"-0.0\"; dtoa mode 0)\njson_dumps | JSON_REAL_PRECISION(0); 0.1  (\"0.1\", shortest round-trip)\njson_dumps | JSON_REAL_PRECISION(0); 0.1+0.2  (\"0.30000000000000004\", 17 significant digits)\njson_dumps | JSON_REAL_PRECISION(0); 1e15  (\"1000000000000000.0\", decpt=16 -> fixed form)\njson_dumps | JSON_REAL_PRECISION(0); 1e16  (\"1e16\", decpt=17 -> exponent form; the decpt>16 boundary)\njson_dumps | JSON_REAL_PRECISION(0); 1e-4  (\"0.0001\", decpt=-3 -> fixed)\njson_dumps | JSON_REAL_PRECISION(0); 1e-5  (\"1e-5\", decpt=-4 -> exponent; the decpt<=-4 boundary)\njson_dumps | JSON_REAL_PRECISION(0); DBL_MAX 1.7976931348623157e308\njson_dumps | JSON_REAL_PRECISION(0); smallest subnormal 5e-324\njson_dumps | JSON_REAL_PRECISION(1); 1/3 -> \"0.3\"; DBL_MAX -> \"2e308\"  (dtoa mode 2, ndigits=1)\njson_dumps | JSON_REAL_PRECISION(2); 5e-324 -> \"4.9e-324\"\njson_dumps | JSON_REAL_PRECISION(17); 0.1 -> \"0.10000000000000001\"\njson_dumps | JSON_REAL_PRECISION(17); 1e-5 -> \"1.0000000000000001e-5\"\njson_dumps | JSON_REAL_PRECISION(20); integral value 1e15  (fits: \"1000000000000000.0\")\njson_dumps | JSON_REAL_PRECISION(20); 1e-4 or 1e300  (rejected: dtostr buffer 25 too small -> dumps returns NULL)\njson_dumps | JSON_REAL_PRECISION(25) or (31); any value needing >17 digits  (rejected, same reason)\njson_dumps | JSON_REAL_PRECISION(31); 0.0  (accepted: short output)\njson_dumps | integer LLONG_MIN (-9223372036854775808) and LLONG_MAX  (20/19 chars, fits MAX_INTEGER_STR_LENGTH 25)\njson_dumps | integer 0, -1, 1\n```\n\n## Encoder — input shapes\n```\njson_dumps | root = empty object {}  (early return at dump.c:328-331, no dump_indent)\njson_dumps | root = empty array []   (early return at dump.c:279-282)\njson_dumps | root = 1-element array / 1-key object  (the n-1 loop runs zero times)\njson_dumps | root = 2-element array  (the only shape exercising both loop body and tail)\njson_dumps | root = object with exactly 8 keys / exactly 9 keys  (pre- vs post-rehash iteration)\njson_dumps | root = array with 8 then 9 elements  (pre/post json_array_grow)\njson_dumps | root nested 100 levels deep, JSON_INDENT(2)  (recursion + deep indentation)\njson_dumps | root containing all 8 json_type values as members\njson_dumps | root = empty string \"\" value  (dump_string with len 0 -> \"\\\"\\\"\")\njson_dumps | string with each mandatory escape: \" \\ \\b \\f \\n \\r \\t\njson_dumps | string with control chars lacking a short form (0x00,0x01,0x0B,0x0E,0x1F) -> \\u00XX\njson_dumps | string built by json_stringn with an embedded NUL -> \"a\\u0000b\"\njson_dumps | object key containing an embedded NUL (json_object_setn) -> key dumped as \"a\\u0000b\"; also with JSON_SORT_KEYS\njson_dumps | object with the empty key \"\" (key_len 0)\njson_dumps | the same json_t appearing twice as siblings (DAG, not a cycle) -> dumped twice, parents-set del at dump.c:300/415 makes this legal\njson_dumps | indirect cycle a=[b], b=[a]  (rejected: jsonp_loop_check -> NULL)\n```\n\n## Encoder — low-level entry points\n```\njson_dumpb | buffer=NULL, size=0  (measure mode: returns required byte count, writes nothing)\njson_dumpb | size == exact required length  (full write, returns that length)\njson_dumpb | size = 3 (undersized)  (returns full required length; only chunks that fit are memcpy'd -> partial \"[1,\")\njson_dumpb | size much larger than needed  (no NUL terminator is ever written)\njson_dumpb | dump fails (e.g. non-container root without JSON_ENCODE_ANY)  (returns 0)\njson_dump_callback | callback that accepts everything and counts bytes  (chunk sequence: each token is a separate call)\njson_dump_callback | callback returning nonzero  (error propagates out of do_dump; partial output already emitted)\njson_dumpf | FILE* to a real file / to a pipe; dump_to_file requires fwrite(...,size,1)==1\njson_dumpfd | valid fd; dump_to_fd requires write() to return exactly size (short writes -> -1)\njson_dump_file | new path (fopen \"w\"); flags=JSON_INDENT(2); return also reflects fclose failure\njson_dump_file | unopenable path  (rejected: -1 before any encoding)\njson_dumps | after json_set_alloc_funcs (no realloc)  (jsonp_realloc emulation path, memory.c:45-61, hit by the final resize in dump.c:438)\n```\n\n## Decoder — flag axes\n```\njson_loads / json_loadb / json_loadf / json_loadfd / json_load_file / json_load_callback | flags=0; input '{\"a\":1}'  (baseline)\njson_loads | flags=0; input '{\"a\":1,\"a\":2}'  (last value wins -> {\"a\":2})\njson_loads | flags=JSON_REJECT_DUPLICATES (0x1); same input  (rejected: json_error_duplicate_key, code 14)\njson_loads | flags=JSON_REJECT_DUPLICATES; input with distinct keys only  (probe runs, no error)\njson_loads | flags=0; input '{\"a\":1,\"b\":2,\"a\":3}'  (key \"a\" keeps its FIRST ordinal position, value replaced)\njson_loads | flags=JSON_DISABLE_EOF_CHECK (0x2); input '[1] trailing-garbage'  (parses [1], ignores rest)\njson_loads | flags=JSON_DISABLE_EOF_CHECK; input '[1][2]'  (returns [1], error->position=3 -> streaming resume point)\njson_loads | flags=0; input '[1] x'  (rejected: json_error_end_of_input_expected)\njson_loads | flags=JSON_DISABLE_EOF_CHECK|JSON_DECODE_ANY; input '1 2 3'  (scalar stream)\njson_loads | flags=JSON_DECODE_ANY (0x4); each of: 42, -1.5, \"str\", true, false, null\njson_loads | flags=0; input '42'  (rejected: \"'[' or '{' expected\")\njson_loads | flags=JSON_DECODE_INT_AS_REAL (0x8); input '[123]'  (-> [123.0])\njson_loads | flags=JSON_DECODE_INT_AS_REAL; input '[9223372036854775808]'  (no longer overflow; -> 9.223372036854776e18)\njson_loads | flags=JSON_DECODE_INT_AS_REAL; input with an already-real literal '[1.5e3]'  (same path as without the flag)\njson_loads | flags=0; input '[9223372036854775807]' / '[-9223372036854775808]'  (LLONG bounds, exact)\njson_loads | flags=0; input '[9223372036854775808]'  (rejected: \"too big integer\"); '[-9223372036854775809]' (\"too big negative integer\")\njson_loads | flags=JSON_ALLOW_NUL (0x10); input '[\"a\\u0000b\"]'  (string value length 3 with an embedded NUL)\njson_loads | flags=0; input '[\"a\\u0000b\"]'  (rejected: json_error_null_character)\njson_loads | flags=JSON_ALLOW_NUL; input '{\"a\\u0000b\":1}'  (rejected anyway: json_error_null_byte_in_key, key check is flag-independent)\njson_loads | flags=JSON_REJECT_DUPLICATES|JSON_DECODE_ANY|JSON_DECODE_INT_AS_REAL|JSON_ALLOW_NUL|JSON_DISABLE_EOF_CHECK  (all five simultaneously)\njson_loads | flags containing encoder-only bits (e.g. JSON_SORT_KEYS 0x80, JSON_COMPACT 0x20)  (ignored; but note JSON_INDENT(n) low bits ALIAS the five decoder flags)\n```\n\n## Decoder — input shapes\n```\njson_loads | '{}' and '[]'  (empty-container early returns, load.c:668/745)\njson_loads | '[1]' / '{\"a\":1}'  (single element, loop breaks immediately)\njson_loads | array/object with 8 vs 9 members  (array grow at 9th; object rehash at 9th distinct key)\njson_loads | object with 40 keys  (two rehashes; insertion order still preserved on dump)\njson_loads | nesting depth 2047 arrays + inner scalar  (max legal: 2048 values)\njson_loads | nesting depth 2048 arrays + inner scalar  (rejected: json_error_stack_overflow at 2049)\njson_loads | mixed nesting of objects and arrays at depth ~1000\njson_loads | all whitespace forms between tokens: ' ' '\\t' '\\n' '\\r' (load.c:574) incl. leading and trailing\njson_loads | input with '\\n' inside so error line/column tracking advances (stream_get load.c:191-199)\njson_loads | number grammar: 0, -0, 1, -1, 10, 1.0, -1.5, 1e2, 1E2, 1e+2, 1e-2, 1.5e308, 0.0001\njson_loads | '[1e999]'  (rejected: real number overflow via jsonp_strtod HUGE_VAL/ERANGE)\njson_loads | '[-0.0]'  (round-trips to \"-0.0\")\njson_loads | string escapes: \\\" \\\\ \\/ \\b \\f \\n \\r \\t\njson_loads | '\\uXXXX' BMP escape, lower- and upper-case hex digits (decode_unicode_escape both branches)\njson_loads | valid surrogate pair '\\uD834\\uDD1E' (high D800-DBFF + low DC00-DFFF)\njson_loads | lone high surrogate '\\uD834' or bad second half  (rejected: invalid Unicode)\njson_loads | lone low surrogate '\\uDC00'  (rejected)\njson_loads | raw 1-, 2-, 3- and 4-byte UTF-8 inside a string (stream_get multi-byte buffering, load.c:167-186)\njson_loads | 2-byte UTF-8 as the FIRST byte of a token outside a string (lex_save_cached path, load.c:623)\njson_loads | 'true' / 'false' / 'null' literals (l_isalpha identifier scan + strcmp, load.c:599-618)\njson_loads | key/value strings of length 0 ('\"\"'), 1, 12, 13, and >1024 bytes\njson_loads | a string whose escapes make the decoded value shorter than the source (t/p pointer walk, load.c:358-451)\n```\n\n## Decoder — entry points\n```\njson_loads    | input contains an embedded NUL  (string_get treats it as EOF; '[1,2]\\0[3]' -> [1,2] with flags=0)\njson_loadb    | buflen spanning a NUL byte  (buffer_get returns the NUL as data -> differs from json_loads; needs DISABLE_EOF_CHECK to succeed)\njson_loadb    | buflen shorter than the strlen of the buffer  (truncation is honored)\njson_loadb    | buflen=0  (premature end of input)\njson_loadf    | FILE* from a regular file, flags=0  (source \"<stream>\")\njson_loadf    | input == stdin  (source \"<stdin>\", load.c:973-974)\njson_loadfd   | fd of a regular file  (1-byte read() loop)\njson_loadfd   | fd == STDIN_FILENO  (source \"<stdin>\")\njson_loadfd   | fd < 0  (rejected: json_error_invalid_argument)\njson_load_file| existing file, flags=0  (note: on SUCCESS error->source is overwritten to \"<stream>\")\njson_load_file| nonexistent path  (rejected: json_error_cannot_open_file, source = the path)\njson_load_file| path longer than JSON_ERROR_SOURCE_LENGTH (80)  (error.c:26-30 \"...\"-prefixed truncation)\njson_load_callback | callback returning 1 byte per call  (per-byte refill; multi-byte UTF-8 split across refills)\njson_load_callback | callback returning 2- or 3-byte chunks straddling a 3-/4-byte UTF-8 sequence\njson_load_callback | callback returning exactly MAX_BUF_LEN (1024) then 0  (buffer-boundary refill)\njson_load_callback | callback returning (size_t)-1  (treated as EOF, load.c:1072)\njson_load_callback | callback == NULL  (rejected: invalid argument)\njson_loads/loadb/loadf/loadfd/load_file | error == NULL  (all error_set calls become no-ops)\njson_loads | valid parse with error != NULL  (error->position set at load.c:877-880 even on success)\n```\n\n## Pack — format characters and modifiers\n```\njson_pack / json_pack_ex / json_vpack_ex | \"{}\"  (empty object)\njson_pack | \"[]\"  (empty array)\njson_pack | \"{s:i}\"  (single key)\njson_pack | \"{s:i,s:i}\"  (multiple keys)\njson_pack | \"{s:i, ... }\" with 9+ keys  (hashtable rehash during pack)\njson_pack | \"[i]\" / \"[i,i]\" / 9+ elements  (array grow during pack)\njson_pack | \"{s:[i,i],s:{s:n}}\"  (nested containers)\njson_pack | format containing ' ', '\\t', '\\n', ',' and ':' as pure decoration (\" { s : i , s : i } \")\njson_pack | \"s\"  (top-level scalar; pack has no ENCODE_ANY restriction)\njson_pack | \"s\" with an empty string \"\"\njson_pack | \"s\" with multi-byte UTF-8  (utf8_check_string on the arg, pack_unpack.c:145)\njson_pack | \"s#\" with (char*, int len) shorter than strlen  (truncation)\njson_pack | \"s%\" with (char*, size_t len)\njson_pack | \"s+\"  (two args concatenated)\njson_pack | \"s++\"  (three args concatenated)\njson_pack | \"s+#\"  (first arg strlen'd, second length-limited)\njson_pack | \"s#+#\"  (both length-limited)\njson_pack | \"s%+%\"  (both size_t-limited)\njson_pack | \"{s#:i}\" / \"{s%:i}\" / \"{s+:i}\"  (length/concat modifiers on an object KEY, read_string optional=0)\njson_pack | \"s?\" with a non-NULL string  (normal string)\njson_pack | \"s?\" with NULL  (-> json_null())\njson_pack | \"[s*]\" with NULL  (element omitted entirely -> [])\njson_pack | \"{s:s*}\" with NULL value  (key omitted entirely -> {})\njson_pack | \"{s:s?}\" with NULL value  (-> {\"k\":null})\njson_pack | \"s?#\"  (rejected: \"Cannot use '#' on optional strings\")\njson_pack | \"n\"  (json_null singleton)\njson_pack | \"b\" with 0 and with nonzero  (false / true singletons)\njson_pack | \"i\" with 0, INT_MIN, INT_MAX  (int-width vararg)\njson_pack | \"I\" with LLONG_MIN, LLONG_MAX  (json_int_t vararg)\njson_pack | \"f\" with 0.0, -0.0, 3.5, DBL_MAX, 5e-324\njson_pack | \"f\" with NaN or Inf  (rejected: json_real_set -> \"Invalid floating point value\", numeric_overflow)\njson_pack | \"O\" with a non-NULL json_t  (refcount incremented; same pointer twice -> \"[O,O]\" shares it)\njson_pack | \"o\" with a non-NULL json_t  (reference stolen, no incref)\njson_pack | \"O?\" / \"o?\" with NULL  (-> null)\njson_pack | \"O*\" / \"o*\" with NULL  (value omitted from the enclosing container)\njson_pack | \"O\" / \"o\" with NULL and no ?/*  (rejected: json_error_null_value)\njson_pack | \"r\" (any position)  (rejected: 'r' is NOT a format char in 2.15)\njson_pack | \"F\"  (rejected: 'F' is unpack-only)\njson_pack_ex | flags=JSON_VALIDATE_ONLY|JSON_STRICT  (both are INERT for packing; pack never reads s->flags)\njson_pack_ex | error == NULL vs a real json_error_t\njson_vpack_ex | fmt=NULL or \"\"  (rejected: json_error_invalid_argument)\njson_pack | \"{s:i}x\"  (rejected: \"Garbage after format string\")\njson_sprintf / json_vsprintf | \"%s-%d\" style fmt producing ASCII\njson_sprintf | fmt producing a zero-length result  (special-cased -> json_string(\"\"), value.c:846-849)\njson_sprintf | fmt producing multi-byte UTF-8; and one producing invalid UTF-8 (rejected -> NULL)\n```\n\n## Unpack — format characters, modifiers and flags\n```\njson_unpack / json_unpack_ex / json_vunpack_ex | \"{s:s}\" on a matching object\njson_unpack | \"{s:s%}\"  (also fills a size_t* length target)\njson_unpack | \"{s:i}\", \"{s:I}\", \"{s:b}\" (on true and on false), \"{s:f}\", \"{s:n}\"\njson_unpack | \"{s:F}\" on a REAL member  (json_number_value)\njson_unpack | \"{s:F}\" on an INTEGER member  (the only numeric-widening format)\njson_unpack | \"{s:f}\" on an integer member  (rejected: \"Expected real, got integer\")\njson_unpack | \"{s:o}\"  (borrowed pointer, no incref)\njson_unpack | \"{s:O}\"  (incref'd pointer, caller must decref)\njson_unpack | \"{s?i}\" with the key PRESENT\njson_unpack | \"{s?i}\" with the key MISSING  (target untouched, gotopt set)\njson_unpack | \"{s?{s:i}}\" with the outer key missing  (recursion with root=NULL: format-only \"skipping\" mode)\njson_unpack | \"{s:i,s:i}\" naming the SAME key twice  (key_set dedupes; still consistent with '!')\njson_unpack | \"{}\" on an empty object\njson_unpack | \"{s:i!}\"  (strict: all keys must be consumed)\njson_unpack | \"{s:i!}\" leaving keys unconsumed  (rejected: \"N object item(s) left unpacked: ...\")\njson_unpack | \"{s:i*}\"  (explicitly non-strict; overrides JSON_STRICT)\njson_unpack_ex | flags=JSON_STRICT (0x2) with \"{s:i}\" consuming every key  (passes)\njson_unpack_ex | flags=JSON_STRICT with \"{s:i}\" on a larger object  (rejected: promoted to '!')\njson_unpack_ex | flags=JSON_STRICT + explicit '*' in the container  (flag suppressed)\njson_unpack | \"{s:i!x}\"  (rejected: \"Expected '}' after '!'\")\njson_unpack | \"[i,i]\" on a 2-element array\njson_unpack | \"[]\" on an empty array\njson_unpack | \"[i!]\" on a l