3.h:206, 290, ~335`) plus a `length>12` loop and a `switch(length)` tail for 0..12 ⇒ key lengths 0, 1-3, 4, 11, 12, 13, >24 hit distinct code.\n- Array: initial `size=8` (`value.c:438-439`); `json_array_grow` `new_size = max(size+amount, size*2)` (`value.c:519`) ⇒ 9th append → 16; a large `json_array_extend` takes the `size+amount` side.\n- `strbuffer`: `STRBUFFER_MIN_SIZE 16`, factor 2, `new_size = max(size*2, length+size+1)` (`strbuffer.c:17-19, 61-79`); measured 16→32→64.\n- `load_callback` reads in `MAX_BUF_LEN 1024` chunks (`load.c:1055`); callback returning 0 or `(size_t)-1` ⇒ EOF (`load.c:1072`). `stream_t.buffer[5]` (`load.c:57`) holds one UTF-8 sequence, refilled byte-by-byte, so chunk boundaries may split a multi-byte sequence (verified OK at chunk=1,2,3).\n- `MAX_INTEGER_STR_LENGTH 25` (`dump.c:26`) — `LLONG_MIN` is 20 chars, fits.\n- `LOOP_KEY_LEN` = `2 + sizeof(json_t*)*2 + 1` (`jansson_private.h:93`); `jsonp_loop_check` (`value.c:47-58`) keys the parents set on `\"%p\"`.\n- `utf8_encode` **accepts surrogate codepoints D800-DFFF** (`utf.c:21-25`, no range check) while `utf8_check_full` rejects them (`utf.c:99-102`) — asymmetric.\n- `json_array_append/insert/set_new` and `json_object_set*` reject `json == value` (`value.c:131, 484, 537, 560`) ⇒ direct self-cycles are impossible; only indirect cycles reach the loop checker (verified: indirect cycle ⇒ `json_dumps` NULL, `json_deep_copy` NULL; same object twice as siblings ⇒ fine).\n- `json_load_file` on success ends with `error->source == \"<stream>\"` (overwritten by `json_loadf`'s `jsonp_error_init`, `load.c:978`); only the fopen-failure path keeps the path (verified).\n\n---\n\n# Part 2 — Configuration-surface rows\n\nFormat: `entry point(s) | configuration`. Rows marked **(rejected)** are nominally-valid-looking configurations that the C actually refuses — included because a port must match the refusal.\n\n## Encoder — flag axes\n```\njson_dumps / json_dumpb / json_dumpf / json_dumpfd / json_dump_file 