json_dumpb | buffer=NULL, size=0  (measure mode: returns required byte count, writes nothing)\njson_dumpb | size == exact required length  (full write, returns that length)\njson_dumpb | size = 3 (undersized)  (returns full required length; only chunks that fit are memcpy'd -> partial \"[1,\")\njson_dumpb | size much larger than needed  (no NUL terminator is ever written)\njson_dumpb | dump fails (e.g. non-container root without JSON_ENCODE_ANY)  (returns 0)\njson_dump_callback | callback that accepts everything and counts bytes  (chunk sequence: each token is a separate call)\njson_dump_callback | callback returning nonzero  (error propagates out of do_dump; partial output already emitted)\njson_dumpf | FILE* to a real file / to a pipe; dump_to_file requires fwrite(...,size,1)==1\njson_dumpfd | valid fd; dump_to_fd requires write() to return exactly size (short writes -> -1)\njson_dump_file | new path (fopen \"w\"); flags=JSON_INDENT(2); return also reflects fclose failure\njson_dump_file | unopenable path  (rejected: -1 before any encoding)\njson_dumps | after json_set_alloc_funcs (no realloc)  (jsonp_realloc emulation path, memory.c:45-61, hit by the final resize in dump.c:438)\n```\n\n## Decoder — flag axes\n```\njson_loads / json_loadb / json_loadf / json_loadfd / json_load_file / json_load_callback | flags=0; input '{\"a\":1}'  (baseline)\njson_loads | flags=0; input '{\"a\":1,\"a\":2}'  (last value wins -> {\"a\":2})\njson_loads | flags=JSON_REJECT_DUPLICATES (0x1); same input  (rejected: json_error_duplicate_key, code 14)\njson_loads | flags=JSON_REJECT_DUPLICATES; input with distinct keys only  (probe runs, no error)\njson_loads | flags=0; input '{\"a\":1,\"b\":2,\"a\":3}'  (key \"a\" keeps its FIRST ordinal position, value replaced)\njson_loads | flags=JSON_DISABLE_EOF_CHECK (0x2); input '[1] trailing-garbage'  (parses [1], ignores rest)\njson_loads | flags=JSON_DISABLE_EOF_CHECK; input '[1][2]'  (returns [1], error->position=3 -> streaming resume point)\njson_loads | flags=0; input '[1] x'  (rejected: json_error_end_of_input_expected)\njson_loads | flags=JSON_DISABLE_EOF_CHECK|JSON_DECODE_ANY; input '1 2 3'  (scalar stream)\njson_loads | flags=JSON_DECODE_ANY (0x4); each of: 42, -1.5, \"str\", true, false, null\njson_loads | flags=0; input '42'  (rejected: \"'[' or '{' expected\")\njson_loads | flags=JSON_DECODE_INT_AS_REAL (0x8); input '[123]'  (-> [123.0])\njson_loads | flags=JSON_DECODE_INT_AS_REAL; input '[9223372036854775808]'  (no longer overflow; -> 9.223372036854776e18)\njson_loads | flags=JSON_DECODE_INT_AS_REAL; input with an already-real literal '[1.5e3]'  (same path as without the flag)\njson_loads | flags=0; input '[9223372036854775807]' / '[-9223372036854775808]'  (LLONG bounds, exact)\njson_loads | flags=0; input '[9223372036854775808]'  (rejected: \"too big integer\"); '[-9223372036854775809]' (\"too big negative integer\")\njson_loads | flags=JSON_ALLOW_NUL (0x10); input '[\"a\\u0000b\"]'  (string value length 3 with an embedded NUL)\njson_loads | flags=0; input '[\"a\\u0000b\"]'  (rejected: json_error_null_character)\njson_loads | flags=JSON_ALLOW_NUL; input '{\"a\\u0000b\":1}'  (rejected anyway: json_error_null_byte_in_key, key check is flag-independent)\njson_loads | flags=JSON_REJECT_DUPLICATES|JSON_DECODE_ANY|JSON_DECODE_INT_AS_REAL|JSON_ALLOW_NUL|JSON_DISABLE_EOF_CHECK  (all five simultaneously)\njson_loads | flags containing encoder-only bits (e.g. JSON_SORT_KEYS 0x80, JSON_COMPACT 0x20)  (ignored; but note JSON_INDENT(n) low bits ALIAS the five decoder flags)\n```\n\n## Decoder — input shapes\n```\njson_loads | '{}' and '[]'  (empty-container early returns, load.c:668/745)\njson_loads | '[1]' / '{\"a\":1}'  (single element, loop breaks immediately)\njson_loads | array/object with 8 vs 9 members  (array grow at 9th; object rehash at 9th distinct key)\njson_loads | object with 40 keys  (two rehashes; insertion order still preserved on dump)\njson_loads | nesting depth 2047 arrays + inner scalar  (max legal: 2048 values)\njson_loads | nesting depth 2048 arrays + inner scalar  (rejected: json_error_stack_overflow at 2049)\njson_loads | mixed nesting of objects and arrays at depth ~1000\njson_loads | all whitespace forms between tokens: ' ' '\\t' '\\n' '\\r' (load.c:574) incl. leading and trailing\njson_loads | input with '\\n' inside so error line/column tracking advances (stream_get load.c:191-199)\njson_loads | number grammar: 0, -0, 1, -1, 10, 1.0, -1.5, 1e2, 1E2, 1e+2, 1e-2, 1.5e308, 0.0001\njson_loads | '[1e999]'  (rejected: real number overflow via jsonp_strtod HUGE_VAL/ERANGE)\njson_loads | '[-0.0]'  (round-trips to \"-0.0\")\njson_loads | string escapes: \\\" \\\\ \\/ \\b \\f \\n \\r \\t\njson_loads | '\\uXXXX' BMP escape, lower- and upper-case hex digits (decode_unicode_escape both branches)\njson_loads | valid surrogate pair '\\uD834\\uDD1E' (high D800-DBFF + low DC00-DFFF)\njson_loads | lone high surrogate '\\uD834' or bad second half  (rejected: invalid Unicode)\njson_loads | lone low surrogate '\\uDC00'  (rejected)\njson_loads | raw 1-, 2-, 3- and 4-byte UTF-8 inside a string (stream_get multi-byte buffering, load.c:167-186)\njson_loads | 2-byte UTF-8 as the FIRST byte of a token outside a string (lex_save_cached path, load.c:623)\njson_loads | 'true' / 'false' / 'null' literals (l_isalpha identifier scan + strcmp, load.c:599-618)\njson_loads | key/value strings of length 0 ('\"\"'), 1, 12, 13, and >1024 bytes\njson_loads | a string whose escapes make the decoded value shorter than the source (t/p pointer walk, load.c:358-451)\n```\n\n## Decoder — entry points\n```\njson_loads    | input contains an embedded NUL  (string_get treats it as EOF; '[1,2]\\0[3]' -> [1,2] with flags=0)\njson_loadb    | buflen spanning a NUL byte  (buffer_get returns the NUL as data -> differs from json_loads; needs DISABLE_EOF_CHECK to succeed)\njson_loadb    | buflen shorter than the strlen of the buffer  (truncation is honored)\njson_loadb    | buflen=0  (premature