{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_dqxdm2nabunmxjnze22kp4pfev72wkslmugokaiud5haarc6hvpa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_016LYYBrEbgUGcvbCs2aEcTR","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Write decoder differential tests","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"Write a Rust integration test file of C-vs-Rust differential tests for the Jansson DECODER.\n\n## Absolute rules\n- Working dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-QfYM1w/translated_rust\n- Create EXACTLY ONE new file: `tests/phase_b_load.rs`\n- Do NOT modify anything else. Specifically do NOT touch `c_src/`, `src/`, `tests/common/mod.rs`, `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `Cargo.toml`.\n- The C code is GROUND TRUTH. If C and Rust disagree, DO NOT fix the Rust and DO NOT weaken the test. REPORT the divergence precisely in your final message.\n- NEVER call Rust functions directly. Everything goes through the loaded `.so` exports.\n\n## Harness already available (`tests/common/mod.rs`) — start your file with `mod common;` then `use common::*;`\n```rust\nlibs() -> &'static Libs            // Libs { c: Library, r: Library }; BOTH already seeded\n                                   // with json_object_seed(FIXED_SEED) at load time\nunsafe sym::<T>(&Library, \"name\") -> libloading::Symbol<T>   // panics if the symbol is missing\ndiff(label: &str, f: impl Fn(&Library) -> T)                 // T: PartialEq+Debug; runs C then Rust, asserts equal\ndiff_n(label: &str, n: u64, f: impl Fn(&Library, u64) -> T)   // property-style randomized runs\n```\nTypes: `json_t { type_: c_int, refcount: usize }`, `json_error_t::new()` with `.snapshot() -> ErrSnap` (compares line/column/position/source/text/code), `.code() -> i32`, `.text_str()`, `.source_str()`.\nConstants: `JSON_REJECT_DUPLICATES, JSON_DISABLE_EOF_CHECK, JSON_DECODE_ANY, JSON_DECODE_INT_AS_REAL, JSON_ALLOW_NUL, JSON_COMPACT, JSON_SORT_KEYS, JSON_ENCODE_ANY, JSON_ENSURE_ASCII, JSON_EMBED`; `json_indent(n)`, `json_real_precision(n)`; type tags `JSON_OBJECT..JSON_NULL`; error codes `JSON_ERROR_*` (e.g. `JSON_ERROR_DUPLICATE_KEY`, `JSON_ERROR_STACK_OVERFLOW`).\nHelpers: `decref(lib, ptr)`, `incref(ptr)`, `dumps_to_string(lib, ptr, flags) -> Option<String>`, `load_then_dump(lib, bytes: &[u8], load_flags, dump_flags) -> (Option<String>, ErrSnap)`, `cs(\"s\") -> CString`, `cs_bytes(&[u8]) -> Vec<u8>`, `cstr_to_string(ptr)`, `libc_free(ptr)`, `Rng::new(seed)` with `.next_u64() .below(n) .i64() .f64_bits() .f64_finite() .ascii_string(max) .utf8_string(max)`.\nFn aliases: `FnLoads = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*const c_char, usize, *mut json_error_t) -> *mut json_t`, `FnLoadb = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*const c_char, usize, usize, *mut json_error_t) -> *mut json_t`, plus `FnDumps, FnSize, FnIntVal, FnRealVal, FnStrVal, FnStr, FnStrN, FnInt, FnReal, FnDelete, FnIter, FnIterNext, FnIterKey, FnIterKeyLen, FnIterValue, FnArrGet, FnObjGet`.\n\n**Always compare BOTH the parsed result (round-tripped through `json_dumps`) AND the full `ErrSnap`** — the error struct is populated even on success (`error->position`), so it is part of the observable behavior.\n\n## What to cover — CONFIGS.md rows 78-138 (read `CONFIGS.md` rows 78-138 for the authoritative list; also read its \"Part 1 / 1a\" decoder-flag provenance section)\n\nGroup into `#[test]` functions, one per related cluster, and label each `diff` with the row number, e.g. `diff(\"row80/REJECT_DUPLICATES\", ...)`.\n\nDecoder flag axes (rows 78-98): the five flags `JSON_REJECT_DUPLICATES 0x1`, `JSON_DISABLE_EOF_CHECK 0x2`, `JSON_DECODE_ANY 0x4`, `JSON_DECODE_INT_AS_REAL 0x8`, `JSON_ALLOW_NUL 0x10`, individually, in the specific combinations listed, and ALL FIVE at once. Include:\n- `{\"a\":1,\"a\":2}` with and without REJECT_DUPLICATES (last value wins vs duplicate_key error)\n- `{\"a\":1,\"b\":2,\"a\":3}` — the repeated key must keep its FIRST ordinal position\n- `[1][2]` and `[1] x` with and without DISABLE_EOF_CHECK; assert `error.position`\n- `1 2 3` with DISABLE_EOF_CHECK|DECODE_ANY (scalar stream: loop calling json_loadb from the returned position)\n- DECODE_ANY on each of `42`, `-1.5`, `\"str\"`, `true`, `false`, `null`; and the same WITHOUT the flag (rejected)\n- DECODE_INT_AS_REAL on `[123]`, `[9223372036854775808]`, `[1.5e3]`\n- exact LLONG bounds `[9223372036854775807]`, `[-9223372036854775808]`, and one past each (rejected)\n- ALLOW_NUL with a `\u0000` escape in a string VALUE (accepted, length 3) and in a KEY (still rejected)\n- encoder-only bits passed to a decode function (note `json_indent(n)`'s low 5 bits ALIAS the decoder flags — test `json_indent(31)` as decode flags)\n\nInput shapes (rows 99-120): empty `{}`/`[]`; 1 element; 8 vs 9 members (array grow + hashtable rehash at the 9th distinct key); 40 keys; **nesting depth 2047 arrays + scalar (max legal) and 2048 (rejected with `JSON_ERROR_STACK_OVERFLOW`)** — build these strings programmatically; mixed nesting at depth ~1000; all whitespace forms (space/tab/LF/CR) leading, between and trailing; input with LF so line/column advance (assert the error line/column on a later syntax error); the full number grammar `0 -0 1 -1 10 1.0 -1.5 1e2 1E2 1e+2 1e-2 1.5e308 0.0001`; `[1e999]` (rejected); `[-0.0]` round-trip; all string escapes; `\\uXXXX` with lower AND upper case hex; a valid surrogate pair; lone high and lone low surrogates (rejected); raw 1/2/3/4-byte UTF-8 in strings; a 2-byte UTF-8 char as the first byte of a token OUTSIDE a string; `true`/`false`/`null`; string lengths 0,1,12,13,>1024; a string whose escapes make the decoded value shorter than the source.\n\nEntry points (rows 121-138) — cover the LOW-LEVEL ones, not just `json_loads`:\n- `json_loads` with an embedded NUL (treated as EOF) vs `json_loadb` with a buflen spanning that NUL (returns it as data)\n- `json_loadb` with buflen shorter than strlen; buflen 0\n- `json_loadf` on a real temp file, and on `stdin` (source should be `<stdin>`) — for stdin just verify the source string via a closed/redirected fd is risky, so instead only assert the NULL-input and regular-file cases, plus `json_loadfd` with a real fd and with `fd < 0`\n- `json_load_file` on an existing temp file; nonexistent path; and a path >= 80 chars (source truncated with a `...` prefix)\n- `json_load_callback` with callbacks returning 1 byte per call, 2- and 3-byte chunks straddling a multi-byte UTF-8 sequence, exactly 1024 then 0, and `(size_t)-1`. Define the callbacks as `unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*mut c_void, usize, *mut c_void) -> usize` driven by a state struct you pass as `data`.\n- every load entry point with `error == NULL` (must not crash, same result)\n\n**IMPORTANT for temp files:** the closure runs once per library, so use a filename that includes which library is being tested or create the file BEFORE calling `diff` and only read it inside. Prefer: create the input file once outside `diff`, then have the closure only parse it.\n\nUse `diff_n` with a fixed seed and >= 200 iterations for at least: randomized valid JSON documents (build them with a small recursive generator producing objects/arrays/strings/ints/reals/bools/nulls) parsed under several flag combinations and round-tripped through `json_dumps` with several dump-flag combinations. This is the highest-value test in the file — make the generator produce escape-worthy strings, multi-byte UTF-8, duplicate keys, deep nesting, and numeric edge values.\n\n## Verify before reporting\n```\ncd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-QfYM1w/translated_rust\ntimeout 600 cargo test --release --test phase_b_load 2>&1 | tail -40\n```\nThe Rust `.so` at `target/release/libjansson.so` and the C `.so` at `cbuild/libjansson.so` already exist and are current; do not rebuild the C.\n\nReport: the number of `#[test]` fns, the number of passing/failing tests, and for EVERY divergence the exact input, flags, C result and Rust result. Do not claim success without pasting the real `test result:` line."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":341,"cache_read_input_tokens":220478,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":341,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c1ef89ae-e696-4035-a7a9-923ffb551939","uuid":"d6d73f7e-54f7-4567-8b8e-9df1c3eeb221","timestamp":"2026-08-14T15:10:43.215Z"}
