{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Fb8gbXfZeEyPpaEoGsmEsU","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# CONFIGS.md — Configuration-Surface Table (Phase B gate)\n2\t\n3\tThe VALID-input mirror of `ERRORS.md`. Every axis below was derived by grepping the\n4\t`if` / `switch` / `#ifdef` branches the C actually takes on each option, not by guessing\n5\twhich configurations \"matter\". Line numbers are from `c_src/`.\n6\t\n7\t## Part 1 — Provenance: the exact branch sites\n8\t\n9\t### 1a. Decoder flags — every `flags &` site in `load.c`\n10\t\n11\t| flag | value | site | branch behavior |\n12\t|---|---|---|---|\n13\t| `JSON_REJECT_DUPLICATES` | 0x1 | `load.c:691-697` | set: `json_object_getn` probe before insert; hit => `json_error_duplicate_key`. clear: `setn_new_nocheck` at `:713` overwrites, and `hashtable.c:243-245` replaces only the value, so a repeated key keeps its **first** ordinal slot in `ordered_list`. |\n14\t| `JSON_DISABLE_EOF_CHECK` | 0x2 | `load.c:867-875` | clear: an extra `lex_scan` must yield `TOKEN_EOF`. set: no trailing scan; `error->position` (`:877-880`) = byte offset just past the parsed value. |\n15\t| `JSON_DECODE_ANY` | 0x4 | `load.c:856-861` | clear: first token must be `[` or `{`. |\n16\t| `JSON_DECODE_INT_AS_REAL` | 0x8 | `load.c:496` — **the only read of `lex->flags`** | clear: `strtoll` fast path, `ERANGE` => overflow error, `TOKEN_INTEGER`. set: falls through the fraction (`:521-532`) / exponent (`:534-547`) no-ops into `jsonp_strtod` (`:551`) => `TOKEN_REAL`. |\n17\t| `JSON_ALLOW_NUL` | 0x10 | `load.c:790-796` | clear: `memchr(value,0,len)` => `json_error_null_character`. Object **keys** with NUL are rejected independently at `:684-689`. |\n18\t| depth cap | 2048 | `jansson_config.h:10`, checked `load.c:779-783` | `lex->depth` increments per *value* (including scalars); `> 2048` => `json_error_stack_overflow`. Not decremented on that error path. |\n19\t\n20\tUnknown/high flag bits are never validated — silently ignored.\n21\t\n22\t### 1b. Encoder flags — every `flags &` site in `dump.c`\n23\t\n24\t| flag | value | site | branch behavior |\n25\t|---|---|---|---|\n26\t| `JSON_INDENT(n)` | `flags & 0x1F` | `FLAGS_TO_INDENT` `:29`; used `:73-87` | n>0: `dump(\"\\n\",1)` then `depth*n` spaces drawn from `whitespace[]` (`:69`, 32 spaces) in chunks of 32 (`:80-86`), so `depth*n > 32` iterates the chunk loop. n==0 falls to the `else if` at `:88`. |\n27\t| `JSON_COMPACT` | 0x20 | `:88` and `:311-317` | `:88` (only when indent==0) suppresses the space after `,`. `:311` picks `\":\"` vs `\": \"` **regardless of indent**. |\n28\t| `JSON_ENSURE_ASCII` | 0x40 | `:123-124` | breaks the raw-copy loop for `codepoint > 0x7F`: BMP => `\\uXXXX` (`:166-169`), non-BMP => surrogate pair `\\uXXXX\\uXXXX` (`:172-182`). Without the flag the surrogate-pair branch is **unreachable**. `0x7F` (DEL) is never escaped (strict `>`). |\n29\t| `JSON_SORT_KEYS` | 0x80 | `:335-387` | malloc `struct key_len[size]`, fill from the iterator, `qsort` with `compare_keys` (`:203-213`: `memcmp` over the shorter length, tie broken by length so a shorter prefix sorts first), then re-fetch each value with `json_object_getn`. Clear => `:388-413` insertion order. |\n30\t| `JSON_PRESERVE_ORDER` | 0x100 | declared `jansson.h:386`, referenced in **zero** `.c` files | **Complete no-op** in 2.15; insertion order is always preserved. |\n31\t| `JSON_ENCODE_ANY` | 0x200 | `:485-488` | clear: root must be array or object, else -1 before any output. |\n32\t| `JSON_ESCAPE_SLASH` | 0x400 | `:119-120`, emit `:161-163` | `/` becomes `\\/`. |\n33\t| `JSON_REAL_PRECISION(n)` | `(n & 0x1F) << 11` | `FLAGS_TO_PRECISION` `:30`; used `:251-252` | passed as `precision` to `jsonp_dtostr`; `strconv.c:75` sets dtoa `mode = precision==0 ? 0 : 2`; `strconv.c:86` uses exponent form when `decpt <= -4 || decpt > 16`; `strconv.c:101-112` returns -1 when the result would not fit the 25-byte buffer (`MAX_REAL_STR_LENGTH` `dump.c:27`, `digits[25]