*(rejected)** | [ ] |\n449\t| 299 | `jsonp_dtostr` | values on both sides of the `decpt <= -4` and `decpt > 16` exponent thresholds; `-0.0` (sign==1) | [ ] |\n450\t| 300 | `jsonp_strndup` | len 0; len < strlen; len == strlen; data containing NUL bytes | [ ] |\n451\t| 301 | `jsonp_malloc` | size 0 (returns NULL by design `:26-27`); non-zero size | [ ] |\n452\t| 302 | `jsonp_free` | NULL pointer (no-op) and a real pointer | [ ] |\n453\t| 303 | `jsonp_realloc` | with a realloc hook (direct call); with `realloc==NULL` (malloc+memcpy+free emulation); `newSize 0` in emulation mode | [ ] |\n454\t| 304 | `jsonp_loop_check` | first visit (inserts `\"%p\"` key, 0); repeat visit (-1); key buffer of exactly `LOOP_KEY_LEN` | [ ] |\n455\t| 305 | `json_object_seed` | non-zero seed (deterministic hashing); called twice (second ignored once `hashtable_seed != 0`) | [ ] |\n456\t| 306 | `hashtable_seed` (exported variable) | read as 0 before seeding and non-zero after | [ ] |\n457\t| 307 | `json_set_alloc_funcs` | custom malloc+free (`do_realloc` forced to NULL -> emulation path everywhere) | [ ] |\n458\t| 308 | `json_set_alloc_funcs2` | custom malloc+realloc+free | [ ] |\n459\t| 309 | `json_get_alloc_funcs`/`_2` | all out-params non-NULL; each individually NULL (skipped) | [ ] |\n460\t| 310 | `jansson_version_str` | returns `\"2.15.0\"` | [ ] |\n461\t| 311 | `jansson_version_cmp` | equal (0); lower/higher major; equal major with lower/higher minor; equal major+minor with differing micro | [ ] |\n462\t| 312 | `jsonp_error_init`/`set`/`vset`/`set_source` | `error==NULL` (no-op); source NULL; source >= 80 chars (truncated); second set on an already-set error (IGNORED `:47-50`) | [ ] |\n463\t| 313 | `json_error_code` | reads the code smuggled into `text[JSON_ERROR_TEXT_LENGTH-1]` | [ ] |\n464\t\n465\t## Notable findings a port must honour\n466\t\n467\t1. **`JSON_PRESERVE_ORDER` (0x100) is referenced in zero `.c` files** — a pure no-op in 2.15.\n468\t2. **Format char `'r'` does not exist*