{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"a2bca285c88547aeb","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_0198oMC6m32rp9eayyEanZQ5","description":"Write pack/unpack differential tests","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"Write a Rust integration test file of C-vs-Rust differential tests for Jansson's PACK/UNPACK (varargs) API.\n\n## Absolute rules\n- Working dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-QfYM1w/translated_rust\n- Create EXACTLY ONE new file: `tests/phase_b_packunpack.rs`\n- Do NOT modify anything else. Especially not `c_src/`, `src/`, `tests/common/mod.rs`, `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `Cargo.toml`.\n- The C code is GROUND TRUTH. If C and Rust disagree, DO NOT fix the Rust and DO NOT weaken the test. REPORT the divergence precisely.\n- NEVER call Rust functions directly — everything through the loaded `.so` exports.\n\n## Harness already available (`tests/common/mod.rs`) — begin with `mod common;` then `use common::*;`\n```rust\nlibs() -> &'static Libs            // Libs { c: Library, r: Library }, both pre-seeded\nunsafe sym::<T>(&Library, \"name\") -> libloading::Symbol<T>\ndiff(label: &str, f: impl Fn(&Library) -> T)                // T: PartialEq+Debug\ndiff_n(label: &str, n: u64, f: impl Fn(&Library, u64) -> T)\n```\n`json_t { type_: c_int, refcount: usize }`; `json_error_t::new()`, `.snapshot() -> ErrSnap`, `.code() -> i32`, `.text_str()`, `.source_str()`.\nConstants: `JSON_VALIDATE_ONLY 0x1`, `JSON_STRICT 0x2`, `JSON_ENCODE_ANY`, `JSON_SORT_KEYS`, `JSON_COMPACT`, `json_indent(n)`, type tags `JSON_OBJECT..JSON_NULL`, error codes `JSON_ERROR_*`.\nHelpers: `decref(lib, ptr)`, `incref(ptr)`, `dumps_to_string(lib, ptr, flags) -> Option<String>`, `load_then_dump(...)`, `cs(\"s\") -> CString`, `cs_bytes(&[u8])`, `cstr_to_string(ptr)`, `Rng::new(seed)`, aliases `FnLoads, FnLoadb, FnDumps, FnSize, FnStr, FnStrN, FnInt, FnReal, FnDelete, FnEqual, FnIntVal, FnRealVal, FnStrVal, FnArrGet, FnObjGet`.\n\n## Calling variadic exports through libloading\nRust supports C-variadic FUNCTION POINTERS. Declare per-call-shape types, e.g.\n```rust\ntype PackI  = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*const c_char, ...) -> *mut json_t;               // json_pack\ntype PackEx = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*mut json_error_t, usize, *const c_char, ...) -> *mut json_t; // json_pack_ex\ntype UnpackEx = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*mut json_t, *mut json_error_t, usize, *const c_char, ...) -> c_int; // json_unpack_ex\ntype Unpack = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*mut json_t, *const c_char, ...) -> c_int;         // json_unpack\n```\nand fetch with `sym::<PackI>(lib, \"json_pack\")`. Pass the exact C arg widths: `'i'` consumes an `int` (`c_int`), `'I'` a `json_int_t` (`c_longlong`), `'f'` a `double`, `'b'` an `int`, `'s'` a `*const c_char`, `'s#'` a `*const c_char` then an `int`, `'s%'` a `*const c_char` then a `usize`, `'o'`/`'O'` a `*mut json_t`, and length/`%` targets on unpack are `*mut usize`.\nKeep every `CString` alive in a local binding for the whole call.\n\n## What to cover — CONFIGS.md rows 139-223\nRead `CONFIGS.md` rows 139-223 (and its \"Part 1 / 1c\" pack/unpack provenance section) for the authoritative list. Label each `diff` with its row number, e.g. `diff(\"row163/s?# rejected\", ...)`.\n\nGround truth already established from the C source (trust these, they are verified):\n- pack switch supports exactly: `{ [ s n b i I f O o`\n- unpack switch supports exactly: `{ [ s i I b f F O o n`; `unpack_value_starters = \"{[siIbfFOon\"`\n- **`'r'` does NOT exist in 2.15** (rejected in both directions). `'F'` is unpack-only. `'#'` is pack-only (`s#` in unpack is rejected with \"Expected format 's', got '#'\").\n- Decoration chars ignored by `next_token`: space, tab, newline, `,`, `:`\n- `JSON_VALIDATE_ONLY` and `JSON_STRICT` are **inert for packing** (pack never reads flags)\n- `JSON_VALIDATE_ONLY` + `{s:s%}` FAILS, because `%` is never consumed\n- `JSON_STRICT` promotes a container with no explicit `!`/`*` to `!`\n- `s?` with NULL yields `json_null()`; `s*`/`o*`/`O*` with NULL OMITS the element/member entirely\n- `\"s?#\"` is rejected (\"Cannot use '#' on optional strings\")\n- `f` with NaN/Inf is rejected (\"Invalid floating point value\")\n- unpack object keys use `strlen(key)`, so keys with embedded NUL are unreachable via unpack\n- a missing optional key (`s?`) recurses with `root=NULL` = format-only \"skipping\" mode\n\nPack rows 139-183: empty `{}`/`[]`; `{s:i}`; `{s:i,s:i}`; 9+ keys (rehash during pack); `[i]`, `[i,i]`, 9+ elements; nested `{s:[i,i],s:{s:n}}`; decoration-only format `\" { s : i , s : i } \"`; top-level `\"s\"`; empty string; multi-byte UTF-8; `s#` with len < strlen; `s%`; `s+`; `s++`; `s+#`; `s#+#`; `s%+%`; modifiers on an object KEY (`{s#:i}`, `{s%:i}`, `{s+:i}`); `s?` non-NULL and NULL; `[s*]` NULL; `{s:s*}` NULL; `{s:s?}` NULL; `s?#` (rejected); `n`; `b` with 0 and non-zero; `i` with 0/INT_MIN/INT_MAX; `I` with LLONG_MIN/LLONG_MAX; `f` with 0.0/-0.0/3.5/DBL_MAX/5e-324; `f` with NaN and Inf (rejected); `O` (refcount incremented; `[O,O]` shares the pointer — assert the refcount field of `json_t` too); `o` (reference stolen); `O?`/`o?` NULL; `O*`/`o*` NULL; `O`/`o` NULL with no modifier (rejected); `r` (rejected); `F` (rejected); `json_pack_ex` with both flags set (inert) and with `error == NULL`; `fmt = NULL` and `\"\"` (rejected); `{s:i}x` (rejected \"Garbage after format string\"); `json_sprintf`/`json_vsprintf` with an ASCII fmt, one producing a zero-length result, one producing multi-byte UTF-8, and one producing invalid UTF-8 (rejected).\nFor `json_sprintf` declare `type Sprintf = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*const c_char, ...) -> *mut json_t;`.\n\nUnpack rows 184-223: `{s:s}`; `{s:s%}`; `{s:i}`,`{s:I}`,`{s:b}` (on true AND false),`{s:f}`,`{s:n}`; `{s:F}` on a REAL and on an INTEGER; `{s:f}` on an integer (rejected); `{s:o}` (borrowed) and `{s:O}` (incref'd — assert refcount); `{s?i}` key present and missing; `{s?{s:i}}` with the outer key missing; `{s:i,s:i}` naming the same key twice; `{}` on empty object; `{s:i!}` satisfied and unsatisfied (rejected, and assert the exact message listing leftover keys); `{s:i*}`; `JSON_STRICT` satisfied, unsatisfied (rejected), and suppressed by an explicit `*`; `{s:i!x}` (rejected); `[i,i]`; `[]`; `[i!]` on a longer array (rejected); `[i*]`; `JSON_STRICT` with `[i,i]`; `[i,i,i]` on a 2-element array (rejected `index_out_of_range`); EVERY member of `unpack_value_starters` as an array element; `[?i]` (rejected); `[%]`/`[#]` (rejected); `JSON_VALIDATE_ONLY` with `{s:s,s:i}` and no value args; `JSON_VALIDATE_ONLY` with `{s:s%}` (rejected); `JSON_VALIDATE_ONLY|JSON_STRICT`; `{s:s#}` (rejected); `{s:r}`/`[r]` (rejected); root scalar with each of `i s b n f F o O`; wrong root type for `{`/`[` (rejected, assert the `type_names[]` string in the message); decoration in the format; `{s:i}x` (rejected); `root=NULL`; `fmt=NULL`/`\"\"`; object with >8 keys under `!` (internal key_set rehashes).\n\nFor every case compare: the return code, the `ErrSnap` (full error struct incl. code and text), and — when a value is produced — its `json_dumps` round-trip AND the values written into the out-parameters.\n\nAdd at least one `diff_n` with a fixed seed and >= 200 iterations that randomly builds a `{s:i,s:s,s:f,...}` pack format plus matching args and round-trips it, and another that unpacks randomly generated objects.\n\n## Verify before reporting\n```\ncd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-QfYM1w/translated_rust\ntimeout 600 cargo test --release --test phase_b_packunpack 2>&1 | tail -40\n```\nBoth `.so` files already exist and are current (`cbuild/libjansson.so`, `target/release/libjansson.so`).\n\nReport: number of `#[test]` fns, the real `test result:` line, and for EVERY divergence the exact format string, args, C result and Rust result.","uuid":"e07760de-061f-42b2-9558-2ce2db6439f9","session_id":"c1ef89ae-e696-4035-a7a9-923ffb551939"}
