|\n| 183 | `json_sprintf` | fmt producing multi-byte UTF-8; and one producing invalid UTF-8 **(rejected -> NULL)** | [ ] |\n\n### Unpack — format characters, modifiers and flags\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|---------------|-----|\n| 184 | `json_unpack`/`unpack_ex`/`vunpack_ex` | `\"{s:s}\"` on a matching object | [ ] |\n| 185 | `json_unpack` | `\"{s:s%}\"` (also fills a `size_t*` length target) | [ ] |\n| 186 | `json_unpack` | `\"{s:i}\"`, `\"{s:I}\"`, `\"{s:b}\"` (on true and on false), `\"{s:f}\"`, `\"{s:n}\"` | [ ] |\n| 187 | `json_unpack` | `\"{s:F}\"` on a REAL member (`json_number_value`) | [ ] |\n| 188 | `json_unpack` | `\"{s:F}\"` on an INTEGER member (the only numeric-widening format) | [ ] |\n| 189 | `json_unpack` | `\"{s:f}\"` on an integer member **(rejected: \"Expected real, got integer\")** | [ ] |\n| 190 | `json_unpack` | `\"{s:o}\"` (borrowed pointer, no incref) | [ ] |\n| 191 | `json_unpack` | `\"{s:O}\"` (incref'd pointer, caller must decref) | [ ] |\n| 192 | `json_unpack` | `\"{s?i}\"` with the key PRESENT | [ ] |\n| 193 | `json_unpack` | `\"{s?i}\"` with the key MISSING (target untouched, `gotopt` set) | [ ] |\n| 194 | `json_unpack` | `\"{s?{s:i}}\"` with the outer key missing (recursion with `root=NULL`: format-only skipping) | [ ] |\n| 195 | `json_unpack` | `\"{s:i,s:i}\"` naming the SAME key twice (`key_set` dedupes; still consistent with `!`) | [ ] |\n| 196 | `json_unpack` | `\"{}\"` on an empty object | [ ] |\n| 197 | `json_unpack` | `\"{s:i!}\"` (strict: all keys must be consumed) | [ ] |\n| 198 | `json_unpack` | `\"{s:i!}\"` leaving keys unconsumed **(rejected: \"N object item(s) left unpacked: ...\")** | [ ] |\n| 199 | `json_unpack` | `\"{s:i*}\"` (explicitly non-strict; overrides `JSON_STRICT`) | [ ] |\n| 200 | `json_unpack_ex` | `JSON_STRICT` with `\"{s:i}\"` consuming every key (passes) | [ ] |\n| 201 | `json_unpack_ex` | `JSON_STRICT` with `\"{s:i}\"` on a larger object **(rejected: promoted to `!`)** | [ ] |\n| 202 | `json_unpack_ex` | `JSON_STRICT` + explicit `*` in the container (flag suppressed) | [ ] |\n| 203 | `json_unpack` | `\"{s:i!x}\"` **(rejected: \"Expected '}' after '!'\")** | [ ] |\n| 204 | `json_unpack` | `\"[i,i]\"` on a 2-element array | [ ] |\n| 205 | `json_unpack` | `\"[]\"` on an empty array | [ ] |\n| 206 | `json_unpack` | `\"[i!]\"` on a longer array **(rejected: \"N array item(s) left unpacked\")** | [ ] |\n| 207 | `json_unpack` | `\"[i*]\"` on a longer array (accepted) | [ ] |\n| 208 | `json_unpack_ex` | `JSON_STRICT` with `\"[i,i]\"` consuming the whole array | [ ] |\n| 209 | `json_unpack` | `\"[i,i,i]\"` on a 2-element array **(rejected: `json_error_index_out_of_range`)** | [ ] |\n| 210 | `json_unpack` | each member of `unpack_value_starters`: `[s] [i] [I] [b] [f] [F] [o] [O] [n] [{...}] [[...]]` | [ ] |\n| 211 | `json_unpack` | `\"[?i]\"` **(rejected: `?` is only handled inside objects)** | [ ] |\n| 212 | `json_unpack` | `\"[%]\"` or `\"[#]\"` **(rejected: not in `unpack_value_starters`)** | [ ] |\n| 213 | `json_unpack_ex` | `JSON_VALIDATE_ONLY`; `\"{s:s,s:i}\"` with NO value args (keys are still consumed) | [ ] |\n| 214 | `json_unpack_ex` | `JSON_VALIDATE_ONLY`; `\"{s:s%}\"` **(rejected: `%` left unconsumed)** | [ ] |\n| 215 | `json_unpack_ex` | `JSON_VALIDATE_ONLY\\|JSON_STRICT` together | [ ] |\n| 216 | `json_unpack` | `\"{s:s#}\"` **(rejected: `#` is pack-only)** | [ ] |\n| 217 | `json_unpack` | `\"{s:r}\"` or `\"[r]\"` **(rejected: `'r'` does not exist)** | [ ] |\n| 218 | `json_unpack` | root scalar with format `i`/`s`/`b`/`n`/`f`/`F`/`o`/`O` (no container required) | [ ] |\n| 219 | `json_unpack` | wrong root type for `{` or `[` **(rejected: wrong_type with the `type_names[]` string)** | [ ] |\n| 220 | `json_unpack` | format with space/tab/LF/`,`/`:` decoration | [ ] |\n| 221 | `json_unpack` | `\"{s:i}x\"` **(rejected: \"Garbage after format string\")** | [ ] |\n| 222 | `json_vunpack_ex` | `root=NULL` **(rejected)**; `fmt=NULL` or `\"\"` **(rejected)** | [ ] |\n| 223 | `json_unpack` | object with > 8 keys under `!` (the internal `key_set` hashtable itself rehashes) | [ ] |\n\n### Value API — objects, arrays, strings, numbers","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_0198oMC6m32rp9eayyEanZQ5","session_id":"c1ef89ae-e696-4035-a7a9-923ffb551939","uuid":"57611fef-b8ab-41b7-b718-a60dcff4aa7d","timestamp":"2026-08-14T15:11:53.882Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write pack/unpack differential tests"}
