{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_dqxdm2nabunmxjnze22kp4pfev72wkslmugokaiud5haarc6hvpa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01C6wh5WD3wAdbB3qkLrbmEm","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Write value API and low-level tests","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"Write TWO Rust integration test files of C-vs-Rust differential tests for Jansson's value API and its low-level exported helpers.\n\n## Absolute rules\n- Working dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-QfYM1w/translated_rust\n- Create EXACTLY TWO new files: `tests/phase_b_value.rs` and `tests/phase_b_lowlevel.rs`\n- Do NOT modify anything else. Especially not `c_src/`, `src/`, `tests/common/mod.rs`, `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `Cargo.toml`.\n- The C code is GROUND TRUTH. If C and Rust disagree, DO NOT fix the Rust and DO NOT weaken the test. REPORT the divergence precisely.\n- NEVER call Rust functions directly — everything through the loaded `.so` exports.\n\n## Harness available (`tests/common/mod.rs`) — begin each file with `mod common;` then `use common::*;`\n```rust\nlibs() -> &'static Libs           // Libs { c: Library, r: Library }, both pre-seeded via json_object_seed\nunsafe sym::<T>(&Library, \"name\") -> libloading::Symbol<T>\ndiff(label: &str, f: impl Fn(&Library) -> T)                 // T: PartialEq+Debug\ndiff_n(label: &str, n: u64, f: impl Fn(&Library, u64) -> T)\n```\n`json_t { type_: c_int, refcount: usize }` (you can read `.type_` and `.refcount` to assert them — do so, refcount behavior is observable).\nConstants: type tags `JSON_OBJECT JSON_ARRAY JSON_STRING JSON_INTEGER JSON_REAL JSON_TRUE JSON_FALSE JSON_NULL`; flags `JSON_SORT_KEYS JSON_COMPACT JSON_ENCODE_ANY JSON_ENSURE_ASCII`, `json_indent(n)`, `json_real_precision(n)`.\nHelpers: `decref(lib, ptr)`, `incref(ptr)`, `dumps_to_string(lib, ptr, flags) -> Option<String>`, `cs(\"s\") -> CString`, `cs_bytes(&[u8]) -> Vec<u8>`, `cstr_to_string(ptr)`, `libc_free(ptr)`, `Rng::new(seed)` with `.next_u64() .below(n) .i64() .f64_bits() .f64_finite() .ascii_string(max) .utf8_string(max)`.\nFn aliases already defined: `FnStr FnStrN FnInt FnReal FnDelete FnDumps FnDumpb FnSize FnObjGet FnObjGetN FnObjSetNew FnObjSetNNew FnObjDel FnObjDelN FnArrGet FnArrSetNew FnArrAppendNew FnArrRemove FnIntVal FnRealVal FnStrVal FnTwoJson FnEqual FnCopy FnDeepCopy FnIter FnIterNext FnIterKey FnIterKeyLen FnIterValue`.\nDeclare any other signature you need locally in your own file.\n\n## FILE 1 — `tests/phase_b_value.rs`, covering CONFIGS.md rows 224-273\nRead `CONFIGS.md` rows 224-273 for the authoritative list. Label each `diff` with its row number.\n\nCover: fresh empty object; `json_object_set_new`/`setn_new` with keys of length 0,1,4,11,12,13,>24 (these hit distinct `hashlittle` alignment/tail paths — use `diff_n` with randomized keys of these lengths); `setn` with `key_len` shorter than `strlen`; keys containing an embedded NUL (ACCEPTED — NUL passes `utf8_check_string`); `*_nocheck` variants with invalid UTF-8 (accepted) vs `json_object_setn_new` with invalid UTF-8 (rejected -1); `value == object` self-insert (rejected -1); re-setting an existing key (value replaced, ordinal position preserved — verify by dumping); inserting the 8th then 9th distinct key (rehash boundary); `json_object_get`/`getn` hit/miss/`key_len` boundary/NUL key; `json_object_del`/`deln` hit(0)/miss(-1)/NUL key; `json_object_clear` then reuse; `json_object_update`, `_update_existing`, `_update_missing`, `_update_recursive` on `{\"a\":1,\"b\":2}` + `{\"b\":9,\"c\":3}` and on nested objects, plus object-vs-non-object mismatch, self-referential `other` (rejected), and non-object args (rejected); the whole iterator family (`json_object_iter`, `iter_next`, `iter_key`, `iter_key_len`, `iter_value`, `iter_at`, `key_to_iter`, `iter_set_new`) on empty/1-key/9+-key objects and with `iter == NULL`; arrays: fresh; append 1..8 then the 9th (grow