{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_016BXq4DrWBV3Sn7LrntMJTg","type":"tool_result","content":"### Unpack — format characters, modifiers and flags\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|---------------|-----|\n| 184 | `json_unpack`/`unpack_ex`/`vunpack_ex` | `\"{s:s}\"` on a matching object | [ ] |\n| 185 | `json_unpack` | `\"{s:s%}\"` (also fills a `size_t*` length target) | [ ] |\n| 186 | `json_unpack` | `\"{s:i}\"`, `\"{s:I}\"`, `\"{s:b}\"` (on true and on false), `\"{s:f}\"`, `\"{s:n}\"` | [ ] |\n| 187 | `json_unpack` | `\"{s:F}\"` on a REAL member (`json_number_value`) | [ ] |\n| 188 | `json_unpack` | `\"{s:F}\"` on an INTEGER member (the only numeric-widening format) | [ ] |\n| 189 | `json_unpack` | `\"{s:f}\"` on an integer member **(rejected: \"Expected real, got integer\")** | [ ] |\n| 190 | `json_unpack` | `\"{s:o}\"` (borrowed pointer, no incref) | [ ] |\n| 191 | `json_unpack` | `\"{s:O}\"` (incref'd pointer, caller must decref) | [ ] |\n| 192 | `json_unpack` | `\"{s?i}\"` with the key PRESENT | [ ] |\n| 193 | `json_unpack` | `\"{s?i}\"` with the key MISSING (target untouched, `gotopt` set) | [ ] |\n| 194 | `json_unpack` | `\"{s?{s:i}}\"` with the outer key missing (recursion with `root=NULL`: format-only skipping) | [ ] |\n| 195 | `json_unpack` | `\"{s:i,s:i}\"` naming the SAME key twice (`key_set` dedupes; still consistent with `!`) | [ ] |\n| 196 | `json_unpack` | `\"{}\"` on an empty object | [ ] |\n| 197 | `json_unpack` | `\"{s:i!}\"` (strict: all keys must be consumed) | [ ] |\n| 198 | `json_unpack` | `\"{s:i!}\"` leaving keys unconsumed **(rejected: \"N object item(s) left unpacked: ...\")** | [ ] |\n| 199 | `json_unpack` | `\"{s:i*}\"` (explicitly non-strict; overrides `JSON_STRICT`) | [ ] |\n| 200 | `json_unpack_ex` | `JSON_STRICT` with `\"{s:i}\"` consuming every key (passes) | [ ] |\n| 201 | `json_unpack_ex` | `JSON_STRICT` with `\"{s:i}\"` on a larger object **(rejected: 