g_set`/`setn` | new value shorter and longer than the old; embedded NUL; invalid UTF-8 **(rejected)** | [ ] |\n| 261 | `json_string_set_nocheck`/`setn_nocheck` | invalid UTF-8 (accepted) | [ ] |\n| 262 | `json_string_value`/`json_string_length` | on a string; on a non-string (NULL / 0) | [ ] |\n| 263 | `json_integer`/`_set`/`_value` | 0, -1, LLONG_MIN, LLONG_MAX; wrong type (0 / -1) | [ ] |\n| 264 | `json_real`/`_set`/`_value` | 0.0, -0.0, subnormal 5e-324, DBL_MAX | [ ] |\n| 265 | `json_real`/`_set` | NaN and +/-Inf **(rejected: the only values a json_t cannot hold)** | [ ] |\n| 266 | `json_number_value` | integer, real, and a non-number (0.0) | [ ] |\n| 267 | `json_true`/`json_false`/`json_null` | singletons with refcount `(size_t)-1` (incref/decref are no-ops) | [ ] |\n| 268 | `json_equal` | same pointer; type mismatch (integer 1 vs real 1.0 -> 0); NULL argument -> 0 | [ ] |\n| 269 | `json_equal` | equal/unequal objects (size then per-key), arrays (order-sensitive), strings (length+memcmp, NUL-safe), integers, reals | [ ] |\n| 270 | `json_copy` | object/array (shallow: children shared), string, integer, real, and a singleton (SAME pointer) | [ ] |\n| 271 | `json_deep_copy` | nested object+array (children not shared) | [ ] |\n| 272 | `json_deep_copy` | indirect cycle **(rejected: NULL via loop check)** | [ ] |\n| 273 | `json_delete`/`json_decref` | each of the 5 heap types; and a singleton (never freed) | [ ] |\n\n### Low-level exported helpers\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|---------------|-----|\n| 274 | `utf8_encode` | codepoint 0 (1 byte), 0x7F/0x80 (1/2 boundary), 0x7FF/0x800 (2/3), 0xFFFF/0x10000 (3/4), 0x10FFFF (4) | [ ] |\n| 275 | `utf8_encode` | codepoint in D800-DFFF (**ACCEPTED**, encodes 3 bytes — asymmetric with `utf8_check_full`) | [ ] |\n| 276 | `utf8_encode` | codepoint `< 0` or `> 0x10FFFF` **(rejected: -1)** | [ ] |\n| 277 | `utf8_check_first` | 0x00-0x7F ->1; 0x80-0xBF ->0; 0xC0,0xC1 ->0; 0xC2-0xDF ->2; 0x