{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_72bfx4xrk7gz4thck2ja2b6hvhfbtmlen4okyp3wuigf22en3tya","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01NzHmYknxKqZawbs93pVEjv","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Write parser error-path tests","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"Write a Rust integration test file of C-vs-Rust ERROR-PATH differential tests for the Jansson PARSER (load.c).\n\n## Absolute rules\n- Working dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-QfYM1w/translated_rust\n- Create EXACTLY ONE new file: `tests/phase_c_load_errors.rs`\n- Do NOT modify anything else. Especially not `c_src/`, `src/`, `tests/common/mod.rs`, `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `Cargo.toml`, or any other file under `tests/`.\n- The C code is GROUND TRUTH. If C and Rust disagree, DO NOT fix the Rust and DO NOT weaken the test. REPORT the divergence precisely in your final message.\n- NEVER call Rust functions directly — everything through the loaded `.so` exports.\n\n## Harness available (`tests/common/mod.rs`) — begin with `mod common;` then `use common::*;`\n```rust\nlibs() -> &'static Libs           // Libs { c: Library, r: Library }, both pre-seeded\nunsafe sym::<T>(&Library, \"name\") -> libloading::Symbol<T>\ndiff(label: &str, f: impl Fn(&Library) -> T)                // T: PartialEq+Debug\ndiff_n(label: &str, n: u64, f: impl Fn(&Library, u64) -> T)\n```\n`json_error_t::new()` with `.snapshot() -> ErrSnap` — ErrSnap compares **line, column, position, source, text, and code** all at once. USE `.snapshot()` FOR EVERY CASE: the exact message text, the line/column/position and the error code are all observable behavior that must match.\nConstants: `JSON_REJECT_DUPLICATES, JSON_DISABLE_EOF_CHECK, JSON_DECODE_ANY, JSON_DECODE_INT_AS_REAL, JSON_ALLOW_NUL`; error codes `JSON_ERROR_UNKNOWN, _OUT_OF_MEMORY, _STACK_OVERFLOW, _CANNOT_OPEN_FILE, _INVALID_ARGUMENT, _INVALID_UTF8, _PREMATURE_END_OF_INPUT, _END_OF_INPUT_EXPECTED, _INVALID_SYNTAX, _INVALID_FORMAT, _WRONG_TYPE, _NULL_CHARACTER, _NULL_VALUE, _NULL_BYTE_IN_KEY, _DUPLICATE_KEY, _NUMERIC_OVERFLOW, _ITEM_NOT_FOUND, _INDEX_OUT_OF_RANGE`.\nHelpers: `load_then_dump(lib, bytes: &[u8], load_flags, dump_flags) -> (Option<String>, ErrSnap)` (uses `json_loadb`), `dumps_to_string`, `decref`, `cs(\"s\")`, `cs_bytes(&[u8])`, `cstr_to_string`, `Rng::new(seed)`.\nFn aliases: `FnLoads` = `unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*const c_char, usize, *mut json_error_t) -> *mut json_t` (json_loads), `FnLoadb` = `unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*const c_char, usize, usize, *mut json_error_t) -> *mut json_t` (json_loadb).\n\n## What to cover: ERRORS.md rows 135-194\n**READ `ERRORS.md` rows 135-194 first** — that table is the authoritative list, with the exact trigger and the exact expected C result (error code + message text) for each row. Write one `#[test]` fn per cluster and label each `diff` with the row number, e.g. `diff(\"row150/too big negative integer\", ...)`.\n\nAlso read the \"Cross-cutting mechanics\" section at the top of `ERRORS.md`. It matters a lot here:\n- **First error wins**: `jsonp_error_vset` returns early if `error->text[0] != 0`.\n- `error_set` appends `\" near '<saved_text>'\"` ONLY when saved_text is non-empty AND its length <= 20; longer tokens get the bare message.\n- When saved_text is empty, `json_error_invalid_syntax` is silently PROMOTED to `json_error_premature_end_of_input` and `\" near end of file\"` is appended — unless the stream is in the UTF-8 error state, which gets no suffix.\n\nCover every row, including:\n- invalid UTF-8 lead bytes 0x80-0xBF, 0xC0, 0xC1, 0xF5-0xFF, and bad continuations / overlong / surrogate `\\xED\\xA0\\x80` / EOF mid-sequence (rows 135-136). Note the message reports the LEAD byte and gets NO near-suffix.\n- unterminated string; raw newline in a string; raw control chars 0x00-0x1F (test EVERY value 0x00..=0x1F individually — LF is a different message from the others); bad `\\u` escapes; bad backslash escapes (test every byte after a backslash); surrogate handling: high+non-low, lone high, lone low (rows 137-146)\n- numbers: leading zero, `-` with no digit, integer under/overflow at exactly `-9223372036854775809` and `9223372036854775808`, `.` with no digit, `e` with no digit, real overflow `1e999` (rows 148-154)\n- bad identifiers (`nul`, `tru`, `TRUE`, `foo`) and stray characters (rows 155-156)\n- object errors: non-string key, NUL byte in key (via a `\u0000` escape — note it fails EVEN WITH `JSON_ALLOW_NUL`), duplicate key under `JSON_REJECT_DUPLICATES`, missing `:`, junk after a member, EOF before `}` (rows 158, 160-163, 165-166)\n- array errors: trailing comma, junk after an element, EOF before `]` (rows 168, 170-171)\n- **depth limit (row 172): build 2049 nested `[` and assert `JSON_ERROR_STACK_OVERFLOW` with the exact message; also verify 2048 nested `[` + a scalar is ACCEPTED.** Test both `[` and `{` nesting.\n- NUL character in a string value without `JSON_ALLOW_NUL` (row 173)\n- `TOKEN_INVALID` and the `parse_value` default branch: `[}]`, `[,1]`, `[:]` (rows 175-176)\n- root not a container without `JSON_DECODE_ANY`; empty input; trailing data without `JSON_DISABLE_EOF_CHECK` (rows 177-179)\n- **entry-point argument errors, each with its own distinctive `source` string** (rows 180, 183, 185, 187, 190-192): `json_loads(NULL)` -> source `<string>`; `json_loadb(NULL)` -> `<buffer>`; `json_loadf(NULL)` -> `<stream>`; `json_loadfd(-1)` -> `<stream>`; `json_load_file(NULL)` -> empty source; `json_load_callback(NULL)` -> `<callback>`. All must be `JSON_ERROR_INVALID_ARGUMENT` with `line=-1, column=-1, position=0`.\n- `json_load_file` on a nonexistent path -> `JSON_ERROR_CANNOT_OPEN_FILE`, message `\"unable to open %s: %s\"`, source = the path; and on a path >= 80 chars -> source truncated to `\"...\"` + tail (row 191)\n- `json_loads` with an embedded NUL treated as EOF (row 182); `json_loadfd` on a closed fd (row 189); `json_load_callback` whose callback returns 0 and `(size_t)-1` mid-document (row 194)\n\nDeclare the extra signatures you need locally:\n```rust\ntype FnLoadf  = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*mut c_void, usize, *mut json_error_t) -> *mut json_t;\ntype FnLoadfd = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(c_int, usize, *mut json_error_t) -> *mut json_t;\ntype FnLoadFile = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*const c_char, usize, *mut json_error_t) -> *mut json_t;\ntype LoadCb = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*mut c_void, usize, *mut c_void) -> usize;\ntype FnLoadCallback = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(Option<LoadCb>, *mut c_void, usize, *mut json_error_t) -> *mut json_t;\n```\nFor `json_load_callback(NULL, ...)` pass `None`.\n\nRows marked `INT` in ERRORS.md (142, 159) are internal/defensive and unreachable through the public API — skip them but say so in your report. Rows marked `OOM` are covered elsewhere; skip them.\n\nFinally add a `diff_n` with a fixed seed and **>= 1500 iterations** that generates random byte strings (mix of: mutated valid JSON, random ASCII, random bytes including 0x80-0xFF, truncated JSON) and feeds them to `json_loadb` under several flag combinations, comparing `(result-dump, ErrSnap)` every time. This fuzz sweep is the single most valuable test in the file for catching error-path divergences — make sure it runs and passes.\n\n## Verify before reporting\n```\ncd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-QfYM1w/translated_rust\ntimeout 600 cargo test --release --test phase_c_load_errors 2>&1 | tail -40\n```\nBoth `.so` files already exist and are current (`cbuild/libjansson.so`, `target/release/libjansson.so`); do not rebuild the C.\n\nReport: the number of `#[test]` fns, the real `test result:` line, which ERRORS.md rows you covered, and for EVERY divergence the exact input bytes, flags, C result and Rust result."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":448,"cache_read_input_tokens":288320,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":448,