{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Pg5Li2CvgyJFeo25ikvyM9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# ERRORS.md — Error-Surface Table (Phase C gate)\n2\t\n3\tDerived mechanically from the C source by grepping every error-return branch\n4\t(`return -1`, `return NULL`, `return 0`, `error_set*`, `set_error`, `assert`,\n5\trange/NULL checks, min/max constants) in `c_src/src/*.c`.\n6\t\n7\t## Cross-cutting mechanics that every row depends on\n8\t\n9\t- **First error wins.** `jsonp_error_vset` (`error.c:47`) returns immediately if\n10\t  `error->text[0] != '\\0'`. A later error never overwrites an earlier one.\n11\t- **Error code lives in the text buffer.** `text[159]` holds the\n12\t  `enum json_error_code`; message is `vsnprintf`-capped at 159 then\n13\t  `text[158]='\\0'`, so the effective max message length is 158 chars.\n14\t- **`error_set` (`load.c:85`) appends context**: `\" near '<saved_text>'\"` only when\n15\t  `saved_text[0]` is non-empty AND `saved_text.length <= 20`. When `saved_text` is\n16\t  empty, `json_error_invalid_syntax` is silently **promoted** to\n17\t  `json_error_premature_end_of_input` and `\" near end of file\"` is appended —\n18\t  unless `stream.state == STREAM_STATE_ERROR` (UTF-8 errors get no suffix).\n19\t- **`jsonp_error_set_source`** truncates a source >= 80 chars to `\"...\"` + tail.\n20\t- **`jsonp_malloc(0)` returns NULL** (`memory.c:26`) — a real error path.\n21\t- **No flag validation anywhere.** Unknown flag bits are ignored;\n22\t  `JSON_INDENT(n)`/`JSON_REAL_PRECISION(n)` mask with `0x1F` and wrap silently.\n23\t\n24\t## Status legend\n25\t\n26\t| status | meaning |\n27\t|--------|---------|\n28\t| `TEST`  | differential test constructs the condition directly |\n29\t| `OOM`   | reachable only by injecting a failing allocator via `json_set_alloc_funcs` |\n30\t| `UB`    | the C performs **no** check (documented above as UB). Calling it would crash *both* libraries, so it is deliberately NOT exercised; recorded for completeness. |\n31\t| `INT`   | internal/defensive branch not reachable through the public API (documented; not exercised) |\n32\t\n33\tOut-of-range `json_type` enum values ARE exercised (`TEST`) wherever the C has a\n34\t`default:` branch, since C enums accept any `int` across the FFI boundary.\n35\t\n36\t## value.c\n37\t\n38\t| # | function | trigger (exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result | status |\n39\t|---|----------|------------------------------------------|-------------------|--------|\n40\t| 1 | `jsonp_loop_check` | pointer already present in `parents` (cycle re-reached) | `-1` | TEST |\n41\t| 2 | `jsonp_loop_check` | `hashtable_set` fails while recording pointer key | `-1` | OOM |\n42\t| 3 | `json_object` | `jsonp_malloc(sizeof(json_object_t))` fails | `NULL` | OOM |\n43\t| 4 | `json_object` | `hashtable_init` bucket malloc fails; object freed | `NULL` | OOM |\n44\t| 5 | `json_object_size` | `json == NULL` | `0` | TEST |\n45\t| 6 | `json_object_size` | non-`JSON_OBJECT` type | `0` | TEST |\n46\t| 7 | `json_object_get` | `key == NULL` | `NULL` | TEST |\n47\t| 8 | `json_object_get` | `json == NULL` or not object | `NULL` | TEST |\n48\t| 9 | `json_object_get` | key absent | `NULL` | TEST |\n49\t| 10 | `json_object_getn` | `key == NULL` | `NULL` | TEST |\n50\t| 11 | `json_object_getn` | `json == NULL` or not object | `NULL` | TEST |\n51\t| 12 | `json_object_getn` | key/key_len pair absent | `NULL` | TEST |\n52\t| 13 | `json_object_set_new_nocheck` | `key == NULL` (value decref'd) | `-1` | TEST |\n53\t| 14 | `json_object_setn_new_nocheck` | `value == NULL` (checked before key/type) | `-1` | TEST |\n54\t| 15 | `json_object_setn_new_nocheck` | `key == NULL` | `-1` | TEST |\n55\t| 16 | `json_object_setn_new_nocheck` | `json == NULL` or not object | `-1` | TEST |\n56\t| 17 | `json_object_setn_new_nocheck` | `json == value` (direct self-insert) | `-1` | TEST |\n57\t| 18 | `json_object_setn_new_nocheck` | `hashtable_set` fails (reha