{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_pd6y5qn2kkbatnxwxr737b2mgk7v7y7a5nbewaaylchekrg35vjq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01PZc4LTABgtZwW9WvB6Msq1","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Write load entry-point error tests","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"Write a Rust integration test file of C-vs-Rust ERROR-PATH differential tests for the Jansson LOAD ENTRY POINTS (argument validation and I/O errors).\n\n## Absolute rules\n- Working dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-QfYM1w/translated_rust\n- Create EXACTLY ONE new file: `tests/phase_c_entry_errors.rs`\n- Do NOT modify anything else. Especially not `c_src/`, `src/`, `tests/common/mod.rs`, `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `Cargo.toml`, or any other existing file under `tests/`.\n- The C code is GROUND TRUTH. If C and Rust disagree, DO NOT fix the Rust and DO NOT weaken the test. REPORT the divergence precisely.\n- NEVER call Rust functions directly — everything through the loaded `.so` exports.\n\n## Harness (`tests/common/mod.rs`) — begin with `mod common;` then `use common::*;`\n```rust\nlibs() -> &'static Libs      // Libs { c: Library, r: Library }\nunsafe sym::<T>(&Library, \"name\") -> libloading::Symbol<T>\ndiff(label: &str, f: impl Fn(&Library) -> T)      // T: PartialEq + Debug\ndiff_n(label: &str, n: u64, f: impl Fn(&Library, u64) -> T)\n```\n`json_error_t::new()`, `.snapshot() -> ErrSnap` (compares line, column, position, source, text, code together — use it everywhere).\nConstants: `JSON_ERROR_INVALID_ARGUMENT, JSON_ERROR_CANNOT_OPEN_FILE, JSON_ERROR_PREMATURE_END_OF_INPUT`, `JSON_DECODE_ANY`, `JSON_DISABLE_EOF_CHECK`, `JSON_SORT_KEYS`.\nHelpers: `dumps_to_string`, `decref`, `cs(\"s\")`, `cs_bytes(&[u8])`, `cstr_to_string`, `Rng::new(seed)`, `FnLoads`, `FnLoadb`, `FnDumps`, `FnDumpb`, `FnSize`.\n\n## Scope: ERRORS.md rows 180-194 (load entry points) PLUS rows 196-198 and 232-240 (dump entry points)\n**READ `ERRORS.md` rows 180-194 and 195-240 first** — that table gives the exact expected result per row, including the distinctive `source` string each entry point stamps into `json_error_t`.\n\nDeclare the signatures you need locally:\n```rust\ntype FnLoadf     = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*mut c_void, usize, *mut json_error_t) -> *mut json_t;\ntype FnLoadfd    = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(c_int, usize, *mut json_error_t) -> *mut json_t;\ntype FnLoadFile  = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*const c_char, usize, *mut json_error_t) -> *mut json_t;\ntype LoadCb      = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*mut c_void, usize, *mut c_void) -> usize;\ntype FnLoadCallback = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(Option<LoadCb>, *mut c_void, usize, *mut json_error_t) -> *mut json_t;\ntype FnDumpf     = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*const json_t, *mut c_void, usize) -> c_int;\ntype FnDumpfd    = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*const json_t, c_int, usize) -> c_int;\ntype FnDumpFile  = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*const json_t, *const c_char, usize) -> c_int;\ntype DumpCb      = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*const c_char, usize, *mut c_void) -> c_int;\ntype FnDumpCallback = unsafe extern \"C\" fn(*const json_t, Option<DumpCb>, *mut c_void, usize) -> c_int;\n```\nPass `None` for a NULL callback.\n\nCover, labelling each `diff` with its row number:\n\n**Load argument errors (rows 180, 183, 185, 187, 190, 192).** Each must be `JSON_ERROR_INVALID_ARGUMENT`, message `\"wrong arguments\"`, `line == -1`, `column == -1`, `position == 0`, and a DISTINCT `source`:\n- `json_loads(NULL, flags, &err)` -> source `<string>`\n- `json_loadb(NULL, 0, flags, &err)` -> source `<buffer>`\n- `json_loadf(NULL, flags, &err)` -> source `<stream>`\n- `json_loadfd(-1, flags, &err)` and other negative fds -> source `<stream>`\n- `json_load_file(NULL, flags, &err)` -> source is the EMPTY string (jsonp_error_init got NULL)\n- `json_load_callback(None, ptr, flags, &err)` -> source `<callback>`\nRun each with several `flags` values, and each also with `error == NULL` (must not crash and must return NULL).\n\n**row 191 `json_load_file` cannot open.** Nonexistent path -> `JSON_ERROR_CANNOT_OPEN_FILE`, message `\"unable to open <path>: <strerror>\"`, `source` = the path. Test: a nonexistent file, a path whose parent does not exist, a DIRECTORY (e.g. `/tmp`), and a path with no read permission if you can create one. ALSO test a path of length >= 80 (`JSON_ERROR_SOURCE_LENGTH`) and assert the source is truncated to `\"...\"` + the tail — build paths of length exactly 78, 79, 80, 81 and 200 to pin the boundary.\n\n**row 182 `json_loads` embedded NUL** is treated as EOF, vs `json_loadb` with a buflen spanning the NUL which returns it as data. Compare both on the same buffer, e.g. `b\"[1,2]\\0[3]\"`.\n\n**row 189 `json_loadfd` read failures.** A closed fd; an fd opened write-only; and an fd pointing at a valid temp file containing JSON (success case, for contrast). To create a closed fd: open a temp file, get the raw fd, close the `File`, then pass the stale fd. Assert the error snapshot matches.\n\n**row 194 `json_load_callback` EOF paths.** A callback returning `0` immediately; returning `0` mid-document; returning `(size_t)-1` immediately and mid-document; and a well-behaved callback that feeds the document in 1-byte, 2-byte, 3-byte and 1024-byte chunks (success cases). Drive them from a state struct passed via the `data` pointer. Also feed a document whose multi-byte UTF-8 sequence straddles a chunk boundary.\n\n**Dump-side rows 196-198, 232-240.**\n- row 238: `json_dump_callback` / `json_dumps` / `json_dumpb` / `json_dumpf` / `json_dumpfd` / `json_dump_file` with a non-container root and NO `JSON_ENCODE_ANY` -> each one's own failure value (`NULL`, `0`, `-1`, `-1`, `-1`, `-1`). Also with `json == NULL`.\n- rows 196, 232: `json_dumpb` with a buffer too small — the C SILENTLY truncates and still returns the FULL required length, and never writes a NUL terminator. Test sizes 0,1,2,3, exact-1, exact, exact+1 and assert both the return value and the buffer bytes.\n- rows 230, 233, 234, 240: a `json_dump_callback` whose callback returns non-zero — sweep the failing call index k = 0,1,2,3,5,10 so the failure lands at different points in the output, and compare the return code AND the bytes emitted before the failure. Do the same through `json_dumps` (returns NULL) so the error propagates.\n- rows 197-198, 235, 237: `json_dumpf` to a FILE* opened READ-ONLY (fwrite fails -> -1); `json_dumpfd` to a read-only or closed fd (write fails -> -1); `json_dump_file` to an unopenable path (`/nonexistent-dir/x.json`, and a directory path) -> -1.\n- row 208: `json_dumps(json_real(1.0/3.0), JSON_ENCODE_ANY | JSON_REAL_PRECISION(31))` -> the 25-byte buffer is too small so `jsonp_dtostr` returns -1 and `json_dumps` returns NULL. Sweep `JSON_REAL_PRECISION(n)` for n = 0..=31 over several values (0.0, 1.0/3.0, 0.1, 1e-4, 1e300, DBL_MAX) and compare every result — some precisions succeed and some return NULL, and the exact cut-over must match. Use `json_real_precision(n)` from the harness.\n\n**IMPORTANT — temp files:** the `diff` closure runs ONCE PER LIBRARY. If a closure both writes and reads the same fixed path, the two runs interfere. Create input files BEFORE calling `diff` (outside the closure) and have the closure only read them. For output files, include a per-library suffix or delete the file inside the closure before writing.\n\nAdd a `diff_n` (fixed seed, >= 300 iterations) that round-trips randomly generated JSON documents through `json_dumpb` at randomly chosen buffer sizes (including too-small ones) and compares the returned length plus the written bytes.\n\n## Verify before reporting\n```\ncd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-QfYM1w/translated_rust\ntimeout 600 cargo test --release --test phase_c_entry_errors 2>&1 | tail -40\n```\nBoth `.so` files already exist and are current; do NOT rebuild the C.\n\nReport: number of `#[test]` fns, the real `test result:` line, the source-truncation boundary you measured, the `JSON_REAL_PRECISION` cut-over you measured, and for EVERY divergence the exact call, arguments, C result and Rust result."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":499,"cache_read_input_tokens":299167,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":499,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c1ef89ae-e696-4035-a7a9-923ffb551939","uuid":"d0e28231-87f5-4b82-8054-f8cb8ac930eb","timestamp":"2026-08-14T15:23:04.326Z"}
