_ENCODE_ANY | JSON_REAL_PRECISION(31))` -> the 25-byte buffer is too small so `jsonp_dtostr` returns -1 and `json_dumps` returns NULL. Sweep `JSON_REAL_PRECISION(n)` for n = 0..=31 over several values (0.0, 1.0/3.0, 0.1, 1e-4, 1e300, DBL_MAX) and compare every result — some precisions succeed and some return NULL, and the exact cut-over must match. Use `json_real_precision(n)` from the harness.\n\n**IMPORTANT — temp files:** the `diff` closure runs ONCE PER LIBRARY. If a closure both writes and reads the same fixed path, the two runs interfere. Create input files BEFORE calling `diff` (outside the closure) and have the closure only read them. For output files, include a per-library suffix or delete the file inside the closure before writing.\n\nAdd a `diff_n` (fixed seed, >= 300 iterations) that round-trips randomly generated JSON documents through `json_dumpb` at randomly chosen buffer sizes (including too-small ones) and compares the returned length plus the written bytes.\n\n## Verify before reporting\n```\ncd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-QfYM1w/translated_rust\ntimeout 600 cargo test --release --test phase_c_entry_errors 2>&1 | tail -40\n```\nBoth `.so` files already exist and are current; do NOT rebuild the C.\n\nReport: number of `#[test]` fns, the real `test result:` line, the source-truncation boundary you measured, the `JSON_REAL_PRECISION` cut-over you measured, and for EVERY divergence the exact call, arguments, C result and Rust result.","outputFile":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-QfYM1w/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-QfYM1w-translated-rust/c1ef89ae-e696-4035-a7a9-923ffb551939/tasks/acf5c247dd541fc35.output","canReadOutputFile":true}}
