tring; string lengths 0…4096.\n- **Entry points (121-138):** `json_loads` NUL-as-EOF vs `json_loadb` NUL-as-data; all `buflen` 0..7; `json_loadf`/`json_loadfd` on real temp files (created once outside `diff`) across 9 input/flag pairs; `fd < 0`; `json_load_file` existing/missing/directory/NULL and paths of exactly 79/80/81 chars plus a 150-char path (source truncation mirrored from `error.c`); `json_load_callback` with chunk sizes 1,2,3,4,5,7,1024,4096 (callback-invocation counts compared too), exactly-1024-then-0, and `(size_t)-1` at four positions; `error == NULL` on all six entry points × 10 inputs × 4 flag sets.\n- **Randomized:** `diff_n` with 448 + 224 iterations plus 220 file-backed rounds, over all 56 (load-flag, dump-flag) pairs. A built-in generator guard asserts the corpus stays healthy — measured 432/448 documents parse, 249 contain `\\uXXXX` escapes, 96 surrogate pairs, 45 duplicate keys, 64 `\\u0000`, 196 raw multi-byte UTF-8, 43 deeply nested.\n\n## Two notes worth relaying\n\n1. **Three of my own initial ground-truth expectations were wrong, not the Rust.** (a) `json_indent(31)` = `0x1F` sets *all five* decoder flags, so `42` parses as **`42.0`** (DECODE_ANY **plus** DECODE_INT_AS_REAL) — not `42`. (b) `TMPDIR` on this host is already 58 chars, so ordinary temp paths hit the `>= 80` source truncation; the assertion now mirrors `jsonp_error_set_source` exactly. Both libraries agreed throughout; only my expectation was off.\n2. **Rows 126/128 (`<stdin>` source) are deliberately not asserted directly**, per instructions — reading `stdin`/fd 0 under `cargo test` can block. The `jsonp_error_init(source)` path is instead covered via the NULL-input branch of `json_loadf` and the `fd < 0` branch of `json_loadfd` (both confirmed `source == \"<stream>\"`), plus the regular-file `<stream>` cases. This is the one gap in rows 78-138.\n\nUnrelated: `tests/phase_b_value.rs`, `tests/phase_c_boundaries.rs`, and `tests/phase_c_oom.rs` appeared in `tests/` while I was 