ump, ErrSnap)` from the C and the Rust `.so`, i.e. identical line, column, position, source, message text *and* error code.\n\n## Notable behaviours pinned down (all C-verified, Rust-matching)\n\n- **Row 135's \"no near-suffix\" only holds for a *bare* bad byte.** With saved_text empty and `stream.state == STREAM_STATE_ERROR`, `\"unable to decode byte 0x80\"` gets no suffix; but inside a string literal saved_text already holds the opening `\"`, so the C *does* append `near '\"'`. The suite covers both placements for all 78 bad lead bytes (0x80-0xC1, 0xF5-0xFF) × 9 positions.\n- **Rows 143 are effectively unreachable as documented**: pass 1 validates the hex digits, so `[\"\\uD888\\uZZZZ\"]` reports `\"invalid escape\"` (row 140), never `\"invalid Unicode escape '%.6s'\"`. The test compares whatever the C emits rather than asserting the ERRORS.md text.\n- **Row 160 confirmed**: `JSON_ALLOW_NUL` does *not* rescue a NUL in an object key — `parse_object`'s `memchr` runs before `parse_value`'s flag check, so the code stays `JSON_ERROR_NULL_BYTE_IN_KEY` with or without the flag.\n- **Row 173 confirmed**: with `JSON_ALLOW_NUL`, `[\"a\\u0000b\"]` yields `json_string_length == 3`, bytes `[0x61, 0x00, 0x62]`, round-tripping to `[\"a\\u0000b\"]`.\n- Integer boundary is exact: `9223372036854775807` / `-9223372036854775808` accepted; ±1 past → `JSON_ERROR_NUMERIC_OVERFLOW`; all overflow cases become valid doubles under `JSON_DECODE_INT_AS_REAL`.\n- Raw control bytes stay rejected under `JSON_ALLOW_NUL` (the flag covers only the `\\u0000` *escape*); `0x7F` is *not* a control byte for the lexer.\n- Rows 166/171 EOF cases all carry the promoted `JSON_ERROR_PREMATURE_END_OF_INPUT`, and `JSON_DISABLE_EOF_CHECK` never rescues an incomplete container.\n\n## Fuzz non-vacuity (asserted in the test, not just observed)\n\n3000 generated inputs (mutate/insert/delete/truncate valid docs, random ASCII, random 0x00-0xFF bytes, token soup, junk-wrapped docs) × 11 decode-flag combinations: **284 parsed, 2716 rejected, 8 distinct error codes** (INVALID_UTF8, PREMATURE_END, END_OF_INPUT_EXPECTED, INVALID_SYNTAX, NULL_CHARACTER, NULL_BYTE_IN_KEY, DUPLICATE_KEY, NUMERIC_OVERFLOW) and **138 distinct message templates**. The test hard-asserts those minimums so the sweep can never silently go vacuous. Every `rej`/`acc` helper also asserts the C's verdict, so no row can degrade into a no-op."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":879,"cache_read_input_tokens":136475,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":879,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Eb9ZRycCcFZfAMyLEwZPmH","session_id":"c1ef89ae-e696-4035-a7a9-923ffb551939","uuid":"46badd12-bc00-4ef3-bffd-3a980e79711e","timestamp":"2026-08-14T15:35:07.708Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write lexer error-path tests"}
