{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a5315067f77468855","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Eb9ZRycCcFZfAMyLEwZPmH","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-QfYM1w/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-QfYM1w-translated-rust/c1ef89ae-e696-4035-a7a9-923ffb551939/tasks/a5315067f77468855.output","summary":"Done.\n\n## What was created\n\nOne new file: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-QfYM1w/translated_rust/tests/phase_c_lex_errors.rs` (~51 KB). Nothing else was touched. (Note: `tests/common/mod.rs`, `SYMBOLS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `phase_b_*.rs` changed during my run — that was other concurrent agents, not me; my suite recompiled and passed against the updated harness.)\n\n**14 `#[test]` fns**, covering ERRORS.md rows 135-141, 143-146, 148-156, 158, 160-163, 165-166, 168, 170-173, 175-179.\n\n## Real test result line\n\n```\ntest result: ok. 14 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.14s\n```\n\n## Depth boundary measured (row 172)\n\nMeasured empirically from the C by binary search over `n ∈ [1, 4096]`, for four shapes:\n\n```\n[array  scalar-inside]: last accepted = 2047, first rejected = 2048\n[array  empty-inside ]: last accepted = 2047, first rejected = 2048\n[object scalar-inside]: last accepted = 2047, first rejected = 2048\n[object empty-inside ]: last accepted = 2047, first rejected = 2048\n```\n\nExactly as predicted: `JSON_PARSER_MAX_DEPTH == 2048` and `lex->depth` counts every VALUE including the innermost scalar/`[]`, so 2047 `[` + inner value is the maximum. `n = 2048` fails with `JSON_ERROR_STACK_OVERFLOW` / `\"maximum parsing depth reached\"`. The boundary pair `(2047, 2048)` is computed independently against each `.so` and compared with `diff`, plus full `ErrSnap` comparison at `n ∈ {2046, 2047, 2048, 2049}`. Also confirmed 5000 *sibling* elements is not a depth error. Runs on a 256 MB stack thread so the measurement is the parser's limit, not the thread's.\n\n## Divergences\n\n**None.** Every case — including the 3000-iteration fuzz sweep and the 2000-iteration × 11-flag-combination sweep — produced byte-identical `(dump, ErrSnap)` from the C and the Rust `.so`, i.e. identical line, column, position, source, message text *and* error code.\n\n## Notable behaviours pinned down (all C-verified, Rust-matching)\n\n- **Row 135's \"no near-suffix\" only holds for a *bare* bad byte.** With saved_text empty and `stream.state == STREAM_STATE_ERROR`, `\"unable to decode byte 0x80\"` gets no suffix; but inside a string literal saved_text already holds the opening `\"`, so the C *does* append `near '\"'`. The suite covers both placements for all 78 bad lead bytes (0x80-0xC1, 0xF5-0xFF) × 9 positions.\n- **Rows 143 are effectively unreachable as documented**: pass 1 validates the hex digits, so `[\"\\uD888\\uZZZZ\"]` reports `\"invalid escape\"` (row 140), never `\"invalid Unicode escape '%.6s'\"`. The test compares whatever the C emits rather than asserting the ERRORS.md text.\n- **Row 160 confirmed**: `JSON_ALLOW_NUL` does *not* rescue a NUL in an object key — `parse_object`'s `memchr` runs before `parse_value`'s flag check, so the code stays `JSON_ERROR_NULL_BYTE_IN_KEY` with or without the flag.\n- **Row 173 confirmed**: with `JSON_ALLOW_NUL`, `[\"a\\u0000b\"]` yields `json_string_length == 3`, bytes `[0x61, 0x00, 0x62]`, round-tripping to `[\"a\\u0000b\"]`.\n- Integer boundary is exact: `9223372036854775807` / `-9223372036854775808` accepted; ±1 past → `JSON_ERROR_NUMERIC_OVERFLOW`; all overflow cases become valid doubles under `JSON_DECODE_INT_AS_REAL`.\n- Raw control bytes stay rejected under `JSON_ALLOW_NUL` (the flag covers only the `\\u0000` *escape*); `0x7F` is *not* a control byte for the lexer.\n- Rows 166/171 EOF cases all carry the promoted `JSON_ERROR_PREMATURE_END_OF_INPUT`, and `JSON_DISABLE_EOF_CHECK` never rescues an incomplete container.\n\n## Fuzz non-vacuity (asserted in the test, not just observed)\n\n3000 generated inputs (mutate/insert/delete/truncate valid docs, random ASCII, random 0x00-0xFF bytes, token soup, junk-wrapped docs) × 11 decode-flag combinations: **284 parsed, 2716 rejected, 8 distinct error codes** (INVALID_UTF8, PREMATURE_END, END_OF_INPUT_EXPECTED, INVALID_SYNTAX, NULL_CHARACTER, NULL_BYTE_IN_KEY, DUPLICATE_KEY, NUMERIC_OVERFLOW) and **138 distinct message templates**. The test hard-asserts those minimums so the sweep can never silently go vacuous. Every `rej`/`acc` helper also asserts the C's verdict, so no row can degrade into a no-op.","usage":{"total_tokens":137626,"tool_uses":23,"duration_ms":759703},"uuid":"8a360b00-6b21-4314-a1c0-7aa6bbbf456f","session_id":"c1ef89ae-e696-4035-a7a9-923ffb551939"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_4wxvqwttc6n7bhsigl667p63oiwkvvff7j5ugy3hyfhfufoq6rja","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_012N1ZaJeccm6tYw5vcshdJw","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-QfYM1w/translated_rust/tests/phase_b_lowlevel.rs","old_string":"        for (i, k) in HT_KEYS.iter().enumerate() {\n            let r = set(ht, k.as_ptr() as *const c_char, k.len(), n_int(lib, i as i64));\n            steps.push((i, r, (*ht).size, (*ht).order));\n        }\n        let full = ht_snap(lib, &slab, ht);","new_string":"        for (i, k) in HT_KEYS.iter().enumerate() {\n            let r = set(ht, k.as_ptr() as *const c_char, k.len(), n_int(lib, i as i64));\n            steps.push((i, r, (*ht).size, (*ht).order));\n            // rehash happens on the way IN, when size >= hashsize(order):\n            // keys 1..8 stay at order 3, the 9th moves to 4, the 17th to 5.\n            let expect_order = if i < 8 {\n                3\n            } else if i < 16 {\n                4\n            } else {\n                5\n            };\n            assert_eq!(r, 0, \"hashtable_set #{}\", i);\n            assert_eq!((*ht).size, i + 1, \"size after #{}\", i);\n            assert_eq!((*ht).order, expect_order, \"order after #{}\", i);\n        }\n        let full = ht_snap(lib, &slab, ht);"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":579,"cache_read_input_tokens":217425,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":579,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01C6wh5WD3wAdbB3qkLrbmEm","session_id":"c1ef89ae-e696-4035-a7a9-923ffb551939","uuid":"f94299f6-0540-48c8-9e49-de1492894d6a","timestamp":"2026-08-14T15:35:10.645Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_des