{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"ad3d538185e10072f","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01C6wh5WD3wAdbB3qkLrbmEm","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-QfYM1w/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-QfYM1w-translated-rust/c1ef89ae-e696-4035-a7a9-923ffb551939/tasks/ad3d538185e10072f.output","summary":"Done. Two new files, nothing else touched.\n\n## Results\n\n**`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-QfYM1w/translated_rust/tests/phase_b_value.rs`** — CONFIGS.md rows 224-273\n- **15 `#[test]` fns**\n- `test result: ok. 15 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.26s`\n- All 50 rows covered. Randomized: `row225/randomized keys x alignment` (400 iters × 15 key lengths × 4 pointer alignments, keys placed at heap offsets 0-3 to hit `hashlittle`'s aligned vs. unaligned read paths) and `rows224-256/randomized mutation sequence` (320 iters × 26 steps of append/insert/remove/set/del/clear/extend/update, comparing `json_dumps` plain + `SORT_KEYS` + `COMPACT`, both sizes, full iterator key order and every return code after **every** step).\n\n**`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-QfYM1w/translated_rust/tests/phase_b_lowlevel.rs`** — CONFIGS.md rows 274-313\n- **18 `#[test]` fns**\n- `test result: ok. 18 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.08s`\n- All 40 rows covered. `strbuffer_t` / `hashtable_t` / `hashtable_list` / `hashtable_bucket` mirrored `#[repr(C)]` from `c_src/src/strbuffer.h` + `c_src/src/hashtable.h`; each struct is handed to the library inside a `Vec<u64>`-backed slab with 128 bytes of 0xAA canary past `size_of::<T>()`, and canary integrity is part of every compared snapshot (proves neither library's struct is wider than the mirror). Randomized: 4608 encode/check round trips, 2600 × (1-6 byte biased strings driving `utf8_check_first`/`check_full` at sizes 0-6 × cp-NULL and non-NULL/`utf8_iterate` at bufsizes 0-6/`utf8_check_string` at lengths 0-6 + a full multi-codepoint walk), 1200 long-string `utf8_check_string` sweeps at every prefix length, 340 hashtable set/get/del/iter_set/clear sequences comparing the full key order after each step, and 560 random doubles × precision 0-17 for `jsonp_dtostr`.\n\n## Divergences found\n\n**None.** Every `diff`/`diff_n` comparison — return codes, `json_t.type`/`refcount`, container sizes, `strbuffer_t.length`/`.size`, `hashtable_t.size`/`.order`/empty-bucket counts, raw key/value bytes, iteration order, emitted `utf8_encode`/`jsonp_dtostr` bytes, `*size`/`*codepoint`/`*out` out-params on both success and rejection paths, and full `json_dumps` output — was byte-identical between the C and Rust `.so`.\n\nI confirmed the tests are not vacuous: temporarily injecting a library-dependent value (an exported symbol's address) into `row224/fresh object` and `row311/jansson_version_cmp` made exactly those two tests fail with `C/Rust divergence in [...]`; the injection was then reverted and both files re-verified green.\n\n## Two rows only partially reachable (documented in-file, not weakened)\n\n1. **Row 292's `key_len` overflow guard** (`hashtable.c:205-208`) is **not safely testable**. `hashtable_set` computes `hash = hash_str(key, key_len)` at `hashtable.c:238` *before* `init_pair` reaches the `key_len >= (size_t)-1 - offsetof(pair_t, key)` check, so any `key_len` large enough to trip the guard first makes `hashlittle` read ~2^64 bytes and segfault — in both libraries. `key_len 0` and embedded-NUL keys are fully covered.\n2. **Row 306's \"read as 0 before seeding\"** is unobservable from a test: `common::libs()` calls `json_object_seed(FIXED_SEED)` on both handles at dlopen time (required for deterministic object iteration order). The test instead reads the exported `hashtable_seed` variable and asserts it equals `0x5eed1234` in both libraries, then proves row 305 by re-seeding with `0x12345678` and `0` and confirming it is ignored.\n\nAlso noted: `jsonp_error_vset` takes a `va_list`, which cannot be portably constructed from Rust, so it is exercised transitively through the variadic `jsonp_error_set` (rows 312-313 otherwise fully covered, including source truncation at 79/80/81/200 chars and the \"second set is ignored\" branch).","usage":{"total_tokens":238130,"tool_uses":70,"duration_ms":1512532},"uuid":"1081af54-0176-42de-aadb-23a463ce0182","session_id":"c1ef89ae-e696-4035-a7a9-923ffb551939"}
