{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_os7on4fv6d7naon4atoxoqsjgoi5sjevyfdbefw7qdnmhgqamjqq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done.\n\n## What was created\n\nExactly one new file: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-QfYM1w/translated_rust/tests/phase_b_packunpack.rs` (3283 lines). Nothing else was touched.\n\n- **20 `#[test]` functions**, **210 `diff(...)` cases**, **2 `diff_n(...)` randomized cases** (300 iterations each, fixed seeds `0xC0FFEE00_00000001 ^ i` and `0xBEEF0000_00000001 ^ i`).\n- **All 85 CONFIGS.md rows 139–223 are covered** (verified programmatically — no gaps); every `diff` label carries its row number.\n- Compiles with **zero warnings**.\n\n```\ntest result: ok. 20 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.01s\n```\n\n## Divergences found\n\n**None.** C and Rust agree on every one of the 210 deterministic cases and all 600 randomized iterations, across return code, the full `ErrSnap` (line/column/position/source/text/code), the `json_dumps` round-trip, out-parameter contents, and `json_t.refcount` fields.\n\n## Notable implementation points\n\n- **`v*` entry points reached properly.** `json_vpack_ex` / `json_vunpack_ex` / `json_vsprintf` take a real `va_list`. Rather than hand-building an `__va_list_tag`, the file enables `#![feature(c_variadic)]` and defines three `extern \"C\"` variadic trampolines (`via_vpack_ex`, `via_vunpack_ex`, `via_vsprintf`) that forward their own `...` onward — ABI-exact for both libraries. This gives full coverage of rows 139/179/184/222 *with real varargs*, plus `json_vsprintf(\"%s-%d\", ...)`.\n- **Independent ground-truth check.** I separately drove both `.so`s via `ctypes` to confirm the tests aren't passing vacuously. Confirmed byte-identical on both: `\"Cannot use '#' on optional strings\"`, `\"Invalid floating point value\"`, `\"NULL object\"`, `\"Unexpected format character 'r'\"`, `\"Garbage after format string\"`, `\"2 object item(s) left unpacked: bee, cee\"`, `\"Array index 2 out of range\"`, `\"Expected object, got string\"`, `\"Expected format 's', got '%'\"` (VALIDATE_ONLY + `{s:s%}`), `\"Expected format 's', got '#'\"`, `\"Expected '}' after '!', got 'x'\"`, `\"Expected real, got integer\"`, `s#+#` → `\"foobaz\"`, `{s+:i}` → `{\"key\":7}`, `{s:s*}`+NULL → `{}`.\n- Also pinned two subtleties the C exhibits and the port reproduces: `{s:r}` reports source `<args>` with text `\"Unexpected format character 'r'\"` because `pack_object`'s `\"NULL object value\"` `set_error` overwrites only the *code/source*, while `[r]` keeps source `<format>`; and top-level `s*` with NULL returns NULL with a *freshly initialised* (empty) error struct.\n\n## Three harness bugs I hit and fixed (not library divergences)\n\n1. Reading `s`/`s%` out-parameters *after* `decref`-ing the root — use-after-free producing different garbage per library. Hoisted all 8 reads above the `decref`.\n2. `row219` scalar-vs-wrong-root sweep compared the raw pointer that `s` writes on a string root; now compares per-slot \"was written\" booleans (concrete values are pinned by row 218).\n3. `rand_unpack_objects` passed value targets while `JSON_VALIDATE_ONLY` was set. Since VALIDATE_ONLY suppresses `va_arg` of value targets, the list misaligned and the library read a target pointer as an object key. Split into a key-only call-site group for the VALIDATE_ONLY flags — which is itself the row 213/214 behaviour under test."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":702,"cache_read_input_tokens":188274,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":702,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_0198oMC6m32rp9eayyEanZQ5","session_id":"c1ef89ae-e696-4035-a7a9-923ffb551939","uuid":"2a1d466c-8e4f-418c-859a-e82e1d361e21","timestamp":"2026-08-14T15: