{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ng4rylpmwj47ysixotyxt6blrbdbtvpl3lumbuag2gz5upr5pasa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All green and stable. Final summary of the work:\n\n## What was created\n`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-QfYM1w/translated_rust/tests/phase_c_entry_errors.rs` — the only file created or modified.\n\n**21 `#[test]` fns**, real result line:\n```\ntest result: ok. 21 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.10s\n```\n(re-run 5×, stable; no leftover temp files, no leaked fds; zero compiler warnings)\n\nCoverage: rows 180/183/185/187/190/192 (argument errors × 6 flag sets × `error==NULL`), 182, 189, 191 (+ truncation), 194 (EOF/`(size_t)-1`/chunked/UTF-8 straddling), 196, 197, 198, 208, 230, 232, 233, 234, 235, 237, 238, 240, plus a 400-iteration `diff_n` `json_dumpb` sweep (measured coverage: 542 truncating / 104 exact-fit / 154 oversized buffer sizes, max document 1451 bytes).\n\n## Measured boundaries\n**Source truncation (`JSON_ERROR_SOURCE_LENGTH` = 80)** — `(path_len, source_len, truncated)`:\n`(40,40,f) (70,70,f) (77,77,f) (78,78,f) (79,79,f) (80,79,T) (81,79,T) (82,79,T) (100,79,T) (200,79,T)`\nCut-over is **79 → 80**: length ≤ 79 verbatim; ≥ 80 becomes `\"...\"` + the last **76** bytes = 79 chars always. The `text` field is independently clamped to 158 bytes.\n\n**`JSON_REAL_PRECISION(n)` cut-over** (first `n` where `json_dumps` returns NULL; failing sets are always contiguous tails up to 31, now pinned as assertions):\n`0.0`/`-0.0`: never · `1/3` & `-1/3` & `0.1`: **22** · `1e-4`: **19** · `1e300`, `DBL_MAX`, `DBL_MIN`, `5e-324`: **18** · `123456789.123456789`: **23** · `2.0`, `1e16`, `1e17`: **25**\n\n## Divergences: **NONE**\nEvery C-vs-Rust comparison agrees. The three initial failures were my own test bugs, not library divergence:\n1. **`json_load_file(\"/tmp\")`** — I expected `source == \"/tmp\"`. C actually gives `source == \"<stream>\"`, code 6, text `\"'[' or '{' expected near end of file\"`. Two ground-truth facts behind this: glibc `fopen(dir,\"rb\")` **succeeds**, so row 191's cannot-open branch is never taken for a directory; and `json_load_file` then passes the same `json_error_t` to `json_loadf`, whose `jsonp_error_init` **overwrites the path source with `\"<stream>\"`**. The path only survives in `source` on a genuine `fopen` failure. Test now asserts this and picks the branch at runtime via its own `fopen` probe.\n2. **row 230 `dumpf_bytes`** — a fixed temp-file name shared by two `#[test]` threads. Fixed with a process-global `unique_path`.\n3. **row 189** — two threads `dup2`'d onto the same high fd 1023. Fixed with a per-call reserved fd slot (`AtomicI32` from 700).\n\n## Ground-truth behaviours now pinned\n- 5 distinct sources over 6 entry points: `<string>`, `<buffer>`, `<stream>` (shared by `json_loadf` **and** `json_loadfd`), `\"\"` (`json_load_file`, because `jsonp_error_init(error, NULL)`), `<callback>` — all with `line=-1, column=-1, position=0, \"wrong arguments\"`, code 4.\n- `json_loads(b\"[1,2]\\0[3]\")` **succeeds** returning `[1, 2]` (NUL == EOF), while `json_loadb(…, 9)` fails with `JSON_ERROR_END_OF_INPUT_EXPECTED` (7); a NUL *inside* a document gives premature-end (6).\n- `json_dumpb` never writes a NUL terminator, never writes past `size`, always returns the full required length, and skips whole chunks that don't fit (so truncated output can be a prefix followed by untouched bytes).\n- Row 227 quirk confirmed and documented in the test: a failing dump callback landing on an object **KEY**'s `dump_string` is swallowed (return value ignored), so the observed call count after a failure at index *k* can exceed *k*+1 — the assertion is `calls >= k+1 && calls <= total` with a comment, not a weakened equality.\n- Failing dumps leave partial output everywhere: `json_dump_file` leaves a partially written file and still returns -1."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":443,"cache_read_input_tokens":154666,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":443,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01PZc4LTABgtZwW9WvB6Msq1","session_id":"c1ef89ae-e696-4035-a7a9-923ffb551939","uuid":"ad68043f-89fe-4858-9d10-ca9ada33748d","timestamp":"2026-08-14T15:41:28.438Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write load entry-point error tests"}
