{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_k76zvgexugo5nqubrf3ipgsmdh6y2ontjxxpphkwzp6i7qr22cga","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01JeVWYt1jVAYTTeEu5hYVcr","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Audit integer overflow panics","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"Audit and fix a specific class of C-to-Rust translation bug in the Jansson port: **Rust arithmetic that panics where the C wraps.**\n\n## Working dir\n/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-QfYM1w/translated_rust\n\n## Absolute rules\n- The C in `c_src/` is GROUND TRUTH and must NOT be modified.\n- Do NOT modify anything under `tests/`, nor `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `Cargo.toml`, `verify_all.sh`, `coverage_report.sh`.\n- Only edit files under `src/`.\n- Do NOT change any observable behavior other than replacing a panic with the C's wrapped result.\n\n## The bug class\nThis crate is a `cdylib` with `panic = \"abort\"` in release. In C, `size_t`/`int` arithmetic wraps; in Rust, `+`, `-`, `*` PANIC when overflow-checks are on (the default for debug builds, and enableable in release). A panic across the FFI boundary aborts the process — behavior the C never exhibits. So every arithmetic expression translated from C that can overflow with **caller-controlled input** must use `wrapping_add` / `wrapping_sub` / `wrapping_mul` (or an equivalent that reproduces the C result exactly).\n\nTwo instances were already found and fixed; use them as the pattern:\n\n1. `src/memory.rs` `jsonp_strndup`: was `jsonp_malloc(len + 1)`. With `len == (size_t)-1` the C wraps to `malloc(0)` which returns NULL, so `jsonp_strndup` returns NULL. Rust panicked. Now `jsonp_malloc(len.wrapping_add(1))`.\n2. `src/version.rs` `jansson_version_cmp`: was `JANSSON_MAJOR_VERSION - major`. With `major == INT_MIN` the C wraps. Rust panicked. Now `.wrapping_sub(major)`.\n\n## Your task\nSystematically find every REMAINING site in `src/*.rs` where arithmetic on a value that a caller can influence could overflow, and fix it to match the C.\n\nFiles to audit (all of `src/`): `memory.rs`, `strbuffer.rs`, `hashtable.rs`, `hashtable_seed.rs`, `value.rs`, `load.rs`, `dump.rs`, `pack_unpack.rs`, `strconv.rs`, `utf.rs`, `error.rs`, `lookup3.rs`, `types.rs`, `dtoa.rs`, `dtoa_tables.rs`, `dtoa_strtod.rs`, `version.rs`.\n\nMethod:\n1. For each arithmetic site, find the corresponding C expression in `c_src/src/<same name>.c` (or `include/jansson_private.h`) and confirm what the C computes. **Match the C exactly** — if the C relies on wrapping, use the wrapping op; if the C has a guard that makes overflow impossible, leave the plain operator (and do not add a guard the C lacks).\n2. Prioritise arithmetic on values reachable from the public API with hostile inputs:\n   - `size_t` params: `len`, `key_len`, `size`, `buflen`, `index`, `amount`, `precision`, `flags`\n   - `int` params: `codepoint`, `major/minor/micro`, `ndigits`, `mode`, `precision`\n   - buffer-size computations in `strbuffer.c` (`size * 2`, `length + size + 1` — note the C has EXPLICIT `SIZE_MAX` overflow guards here, at `strbuffer.c:66-69`; make sure the Rust reproduces those guards AND does not panic while evaluating them)\n   - `hashtable.c` `init_pair`'s guard `key_len >= (size_t)-1 - offsetof(pair_t, key)` and the `offsetof + key_len + 1` allocation\n   - `value.c` `json_array_grow`'s `max(size + amount, size * 2)`\n   - `dump.c` `dump_to_buffer`'s `buf->used + size`\n   - `dtoa.rs`'s many `u64`/`i32` bit computations — these were translated from C code that wraps freely; check especially shift amounts and any `<<`/`>>` with a variable count (C is UB past the width, x86-64 masks mod 64; Rust panics in debug). The file already has `sl`/`sr` helpers using `wrapping_shl`/`wrapping_shr` — use them where a variable shift count could reach or exceed the width.\n3. Also check for potential **slice/array index panics** where the C would do an unchecked read, and for `as` casts that Rust would not panic on but that change value vs C.\n\nPrefer the minimal, most local change. Add a short comment at each site explaining what the C does and why the wrapping op is required, in the style of the two existing fixes.\n\n## Verify your work\nThe full differential test suite must stay green in BOTH profiles (debug has overflow-checks ON, which is what exposes this bug class):\n```\ncd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-QfYM1w/translated_rust\ntimeout 600 cargo build 2>&1 | tail -5\ntimeout 600 cargo build --release 2>&1 | tail -5\ntimeout 600 cargo test 2>&1 | grep -E \"^test result|panicked at src/|attempt to\"\ntimeout 600 cargo test --release 2>&1 | grep -E \"^test result|panicked at src/\"\n```\nThere are 12 test binaries; every one must report `test result: ok`. Current totals: 164 tests in debug, 164 in release, all passing — do not regress them.\n\nALSO run the release differential driver, which must remain byte-identical (75420 lines, 0 differences):\n```\ngcc -O1 -o /tmp/dd tests_c/diff_driver.c -ldl\n/tmp/dd $PWD/cbuild/libjansson.so > /tmp/c.txt\n/tmp/dd $PWD/target/release/libjansson.so > /tmp/r.txt\ndiff /tmp/c.txt /tmp/r.txt | grep -c '^[<>]'   # must print 0\n```\n\nAs an extra sweep, build and test the RELEASE profile with overflow checks forced on, which turns this latent bug class into hard failures across the whole randomized suite:\n```\nRUSTFLAGS=\"-C overflow-checks=on\" timeout 600 cargo test --release 2>&1 | grep -E \"^test result|panicked at src/|attempt to\"\n```\nReport that command's full results — that sweep is the real measure of whether you found everything. If it reveals panics, fix them and re-run until clean.\n\nReport: every site you changed (file:line, the C expression, the Rust before/after), every site you deliberately left alone and why, and the final results of all the commands above with real output. Do not claim success without pasting the actual `test result:` lines and the `diff | grep -c` count."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":837,"cache_read_input_tokens":389555,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":837,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c1ef89ae-e696-4035-a7a9-923ffb551939","uuid":"e0258b85-fe73-4d99-85d6-8f59ab79528c","timestamp":"2026-08-14T15:49:23.229Z"}
